{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:21:06.773Z","ordinal":34940,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","session_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","root_turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","response_id":"resp_0fd4138577b17921016ae847ee796c81a39210846b469511bd","usage":{"input_tokens":80453,"cached_input_tokens":79360,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":454,"reasoning_output_tokens":328,"total_tokens":80907},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6235707,"cached_input_tokens":6079872,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":17614,"reasoning_output_tokens":2374,"total_tokens":6253321},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":665640651,"cached_input_tokens":659656704,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1416029,"reasoning_output_tokens":725848,"total_tokens":667056680}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:21:09.494Z","ordinal":34941,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2a9022d0-036a-4895-bb74-149652b7b3ed","process_id":"87136","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,240p' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md; rg -n 'AC4|G1.1-2|six tasks|six-task|v1.1.2' docs/v1.1.0 docs/v1.1.2"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,240p' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md","name":"WP-1104-PLAN.md","path":"docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'AC4|G1.1-2|six tasks|six-task|v1.1.2' docs/v1.1.0 docs/v1.1.2","query":"AC4|G1.1-2|six tasks|six-task|v1.1.2","path":"v1.1.0"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"# WP-1104: Standalone `nexus eval` command\n\n## Specification\n\n**User story:** As a Nexus operator, I need to run a versioned evaluation dataset through the installed Nexus executable and receive a structured score file, so that I can compare candidate builds reproducibly without depending on the source checkout.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:**\n\n- **AC1:** `nexus eval --help` exposes `--dataset`, `--split`, `--runs`, `--isolated-home`, and `--output`. Test: `eval CLI help exposes versioned dataset options`.\n- **AC2:** A packaged candidate resolves and executes the installed CLI dispatch, runner, and scorer from its package closure when launched outside the source checkout, without inference for an empty benchmark split. Test: `packaged evaluator runtime executes outside checkout`.\n- **AC3:** A versioned dataset run rejects unsupported `--limit` before creating the output directory or starting the runner; help states that `--limit` applies only to legacy runs. Test: `versioned eval rejects limit before runner or output creation`.\n- **AC4:** An exact installed candidate run executes the six unique public benchmark tasks with no skips or missing tasks and records the binary SHA, split, and recomputed manifest SHA. Test: `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance`.\n- **AC5:** Existing legacy dataset invocation and `--limit` behavior remain compatible. Test: `legacy eval invocation and limit remain supported`.\n\n**Out of scope:** Adding evaluator kinds, changing the public dataset schema, changing legacy scoring, or publishing/tagging a release.\n\n**Dependencies:** WP-1103 versioned dataset and runner foundation at `6adbeb31` and `00a8cb4d` on this branch. WP-1102 is not a functional dependency. WP-1108 is not imported as a branch; package changes will be based on the selected current package script and separately checked against its ownership and gate state.\n\n**Files claimed:** `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`, `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs`, `eval/README.md`, `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs`, `scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md`, and all paths in the accepted WP-1103 commits being integrated.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. **CLI grammar and compatibility** — files: `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`; tests: `eval CLI help exposes versioned dataset options`, `legacy eval invocation and limit remain supported`. Write tests first, verify expected RED, then port the CLI implementation.\n2. **Versioned argument validation** — files: `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`; test: `versioned eval rejects limit before runner or output creation`. Preserve existing runner and filesystem behavior outside this acceptance criterion.\n3. **Versioned runtime dispatch and packaged closure** — files: `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/README.md`, `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs`, `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs`, `scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`; tests: `versioned eval invokes resolved installed runner`, `evaluator runtime allowlist copies only runtime files`, `packaged evaluator runtime executes outside checkout`. First verify resolver/dispatch with a synthetic package; verify the staged allowlist excludes datasets/oracles; then build and stage the actual package and invoke the installed CLI outside the checkout against an empty benchmark split, exercising the real runner and scorer subprocesses without inference. Reconcile package allowlist changes against the current script rather than replaying historical packaging commits.\n4. **Installed candidate acceptance** — files: `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts` and the WP-1103 acceptance evidence path when claimed; test: `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance`. Require six unique manifest IDs, an invocation and validator result for each, zero skips/missing, candidate binary SHA, split, and recomputed manifest SHA.\n\n**Reference corpora:** `nexus-cli` for Commander registration and CLI command dispatch; `nexus-test` for CLI command test patterns; `nexus-wp1104-reference` for the prior WP-1104 resolver and runtime behavior; `nexus-docs` for evaluation acceptance and dataset contracts.\n\n**Risk / unknowns:** The current package script must contain the evaluator closure needed by WP-1105. Retrieval query: \"which evaluator modules are copied into the Linux package and how are runtime paths resolved?\" The installed artifact test is the acceptance gate for this boundary.\n\n## Base and claim state at plan review\n\n- Selected source base: `origin/main` = `593d569b5aa2a43d1b31138d37e90b8b65ffcbe7`.\n- Current package script blob at that base: `5f410376b1c167fa6422ea912d8e69e92ccb8972`.\n- `scripts/package-linux.sh` claim was free before this slice took its claim.\n- WP-1108 triage at `v1/wp-1108-dependency-modernization` says its added CI job has not run at that branch head and its policy batch is not accepted; no WP-1108 packaging changes are treated as a qualified prerequisite.\n- Plan review: approved after narrowing dependencies, adding RED-first named tests, and requiring real package execution outside the checkout.\n\n## Retrieval log\n\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-cli`; query: \"Commander CLI command registration subcommand options action parse\"; hit `index.ts:2`; Commander import and command registration context informed the planned integration seam.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-cli`; definition lookup `createCommand`; MISS. No eval-specific API was derived from this lookup.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-cli`; query: \"registerOperationCommands program.command run resume status options action\"; hit `operation_cli.ts:230`; retrieved the `Command` parameter and chained `.command(...).option(...).action(...)` registration pattern.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-test`; query: \"CLI parser help assert spawnSync process execPath test\"; hit `cli_option_scope.test.ts:29`; retrieved the real CLI invocation/help assertion pattern.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-wp1104-reference`; query: \"parseEvalRuns and validate versioned dataset options runVersionedEvalCommand\"; hit `eval_cli.ts:254`; the prior runner validates required dataset and rejects versioned `--limit` before resolving the installed runner or creating output.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-wp1104-reference`; query: \"resolveInstalledEvalRuntime NEXUS_HOME packageRoot runnerApiPath installed executable path\"; hit `eval_cli.ts:228`; installed resolver uses `NEXUS_HOME`, canonicalizes the launcher/runtime paths, checks package confinement and executable status.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-wp1104-reference`; query: \"isolateEvalCommandHome HOME XDG eval command startup before provider config\"; hit `eval_cli.ts:160`; isolated HOME and XDG paths are set before launcher configuration/startup.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-wp1104-reference`; query: \"resolveInstalledEvalRuntime NEXUS_HOME packageRoot runnerApiPath installed executable path\"; definition hit `eval_cli.ts:228`; signature accepts an injectable environment for deterministic resolver tests.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-wp1104-package-reference`; query: \"package-linux.sh evaluator runtime allowlist copy eval run.mjs\"; hit `package-linux.sh:73`; retrieved the explicit runtime closure and exclusions for datasets, tests and held-out payloads.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-test`; query: \"http createServer mock OpenAI chat completions endpoint request capture test\"; hit `cloud_providers.test.ts:34`; retrieved the local mock-server pattern with ephemeral loopback binding and captured JSON request bodies for the strengthened non-empty legacy `--limit` regression.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-test`; query: \"text/event-stream choices delta finish_reason DONE mock completion stream server test\"; hit `local_request_params.test.ts:31`; retrieved the SSE response contract used by the agent client: assistant delta, terminal `finish_reason`, then `[DONE]`.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-wp1104-reference`; query: \"run.mjs creates results.jsonl output directory before appending task records\"; no relevant hit because the indexed prefix contains `cli/src` only. The failing outside-checkout test showed that an empty versioned split invokes the scorer with no `results.jsonl`; the fix initializes the new results file before appending records, following the existing file/append flow in `eval/run.mjs`.\n\n## TDD evidence\n\n- **RED:** `eval CLI help exposes versioned dataset options` failed on the expected missing `--dataset` option in the existing CLI help.\n- **RED:** `versioned eval rejects limit before runner or output creation` failed on the expected unrecognized versioned CLI options before the validation was added.\n- **RED:** `versioned eval invokes resolved installed runner` failed because the old legacy evaluator attempted to read the versioned dataset directory as a file (`EISDIR`).\n- **GREEN:** `npm run build` passed; the initial `node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/eval_cli.test.ts` run passed 7/7 with the original empty-dataset legacy case. That test was later strengthened because the initial case did not prove truncation.\n- **RED:** `evaluator runtime allowlist copies only runtime files` failed on the expected empty scaffold allowlist; `evaluator runtime staging fails when an allowlisted module is missing` failed because the scaffold did not validate required files.\n- **RED:** Strengthened `packaged evaluator runtime executes outside checkout` to invoke the packaged CLI and actual runner/scorer against a valid empty dataset; it failed because `eval/run.mjs` did not create `results.jsonl` when the selected split had no tasks.\n- **GREEN:** Pinned Bookworm package build completed; after extraction outside the checkout, `node --test eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` passed 3/3 with the actual installed `nexus eval` CLI, runner, and scorer. The rebuilt development artifact is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.1.tar.gz`; it is not exact-commit release evidence.\n- **Peer review:** Independent code review returned `APPROVED_WITH_COMMENTS` for AC2. Reviewer confirmed the installed CLI/runner/scorer path and the empty-split file fix; the comment is blocking AC4 evidence, which remains outstanding.\n- **AC3 test review:** A second independent read-only review confirmed that passing an invalid `NEXUS_HOME` and asserting the explicit `--limit` diagnostic wins establishes validation-before-runtime-resolution; assertions cover the score parent, score file and artifact directory remaining absent. The focused test has not yet been run because another worktree's test process is still live.\n- **AC5 test review:** An independent read-only review confirmed the non-empty two-task fixture and `--limit 1` assertions exercise real truncation and first-task-only prompting. The reviewer caught that `spawnSync` would block the in-process mock server; the test now uses async `spawn`, which the reviewer confirmed resolves that deadlock. Runtime verification remains pending the shared test lane.\n- **AC5 red/green:** The first strengthened run failed because the mock returned JSON while the client requested SSE (`INFERENCE_FAILED: stream_incomplete`). After switching to the retrieved SSE contract and setting `--workspace` to an isolated empty directory (so evaluator discovery cannot run this repository's test suite), `node cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs test/eval_cli.test.ts` passed 7/7; the non-empty `--limit 1` case confirmed exactly one completion request containing the first prompt and not the second.\n\n## Gate attempt notes\n\n- **Global release-scope guard:** Current `docs/releases/v1.1.2.md` still defines v1.1.2 as a patch on v1.1.1 containing one operation-message fix and inheriting v1.1.1 qualification. `docs/v1.1.0/README.md` also says WP-11xx is not implemented in its described release. This conflicts with the user's direction to complete the full WP-1101..WP-1108 roadmap in v1.1.2. The release definition, integrated branch, qualification and candidate must be reconciled to the full roadmap before any v1.1.2 publication; this WP slice does not change the release notes or release branch.\n- **Cross-slice audit (2026-11-02, independent read-only agents):** WP-1101 (`8a83c9e7`) has an unintegrated recorder prototype without runtime event wiring or branch-head gate evidence; WP-1102 (`ee7c8b1e`) has partial redaction work with operator acceptance pending; WP-1103 dataset/runner branches (`e430dab5`, `c548e53e`) have no PR, and required actual provider-request isolation, filesystem/mount denial, post-exit oracle scoring, and six-task G1.1-2 evidence are absent. WP-1105 has no implementation delta, WP-1106 has no branch or implementation, WP-1107 (`9cb5f6de`) is an unintegrated grammar generator prototype without provider-path integration, and WP-1108 (`550112cd`) is a partial modernization policy batch without branch-head gate evidence. None is release-qualified. These are audit leads; revalidate on the integrated exact head before marking any tracker item done.\n\n- A first `npm test` run on `/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-suite-snapshot` was diagnostic only: the snapshot had no `cli/dist/index.js` or Rust core binaries, and `NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT` was unset so the actual package smoke was skipped. Its test runner reported 1,981 tests (1,739 pass, 222 fail) and then remained in `turn_semantics.test.ts` with repeated provider-recovery retries; that process was interrupted after about 40 minutes. This is not accepted full-suite evidence.\n- Snapshot prerequisites are now built: `npm run build` and debug `cargo build --locked --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui` passed. Release core binaries were copied from the successful pinned Bookworm package build, whose Rust sources are unchanged by this WP-1104 slice.\n- A separate focused test process in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/pr398-review` remains active. The next full-suite attempt must wait for it to finish, then set `NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT` to the freshly extracted development package so the actual outside-checkout runtime test runs instead of skipping.\n- After peer review identified that the former empty-dataset `--limit 0` case did not prove truncation, the legacy compatibility test was strengthened to a non-empty two-task fixture and async local OpenAI-compatible mock. The first mock response format caused an expected transport failure; the second run timed out because the evaluator used the repository as its workspace and discovered the repository test command. Both causes were corrected. Current targeted TypeScript no-emit and `git diff --check` pass, and the updated focused suite passes 7/7.\n- AC4 can use the deterministic local fake provider and payload capture specified in `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md`; no public provider is needed for the dataset-isolation acceptance. The release concurrency plan still requires the serial `GATEWAY` claim for evaluator runs. That claim is held by `codex-root` on `ubuntu-desktop` for RC15 E5 provider verification (since 2026-10-31T09:47Z, no PID). This host is `mike-dev`, has a different boot ID, and has no matching process; the claimed worktree remains with untracked RC15 evidence. A handoff/stale determination is not supportable locally, so a conflict/handoff request was appended to the shared claim log and the claim/worktree remain untouched.\nrg: docs/v1.1.2: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md:56:- **Gate G1.1-2 (Dataset Decoupling):** Evaluator executes 100% of benchmark tasks with zero leakage of `oracles.jsonl` to agent prompt context.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:13:- **AC4:** After the candidate exits, the evaluator can still access the private oracle record and produce the expected score for the synthetic fixture. Test: `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:18:**Dependencies:** WP-1103 versioned dataset loader and runner integration; current runner claims are held by root after the prior claim was recorded stale and broken; a test seam for AC1, AC2 and AC4. AC5 requires an integrated exact-candidate benchmark run and is separate from the unit regression suite; packaged installed CLI behavior depends on WP-1104.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:20:**Files claimed/current ownership:** The plan file and `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs` are claimed by root on `v1/v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` at `origin/main` 593d569b. The WP-1103 umbrella claim covers `eval/dataset.mjs`, `eval/datasets/core-v1/**` (public development tasks only), `eval/README.md`, and `docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md`. Runner claims on the same branch cover `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/runner_integrity.mjs`, and `eval/dataset.test.mjs`; that `eval/dataset.test.mjs` claim spans chunks 1 and 2 sequentially. The G1.1-2 evidence is claimed at `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`; write it only after the exact candidate CLI run completes and the final manifest hash is recomputed. Do not edit, index, or expose held-out payloads.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:26:3. **Prove candidate isolation and complete coverage** — use the actual candidate CLI path with a deterministic local fake provider that captures the request after prompt construction. Separately intercept and record the exact `{command, argv, env}` launch payload handed to the sandbox wrapper, and inspect the sandbox payload/stdin at that boundary. Assert the objective appears in the expected argv and captured provider request; the sentinel is absent from serialized argv/environment/stdin; and credentials stay evaluator-side except the intended local proxy token. Keep filesystem/mount checks in the separate `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` test. Score with evaluator-held oracles after candidate exit. Then run every manifest-declared benchmark ID with no skips, recording candidate SHA, dataset/split, recomputed manifest hash, request capture and validator/scorer result in the claimed `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`. Tests/evidence: `versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels`; `candidate launch envelope contains stimulus but no oracle data in argv env or stdin`; `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`; `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`; `versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage`. Requires the installed candidate and package closure from WP-1104; this is the G1.1-2 evidence run, not a unit-test substitute.\ndocs/v1.1.0/QUALITY_PLAN.md:11:- AC4: A future task envelope containing an invalid nested operation reports the envelope-version error before nested interpretation, leaves bytes and mtime unchanged, and creates no backup or quarantine sidecar → test: `replay refuses a future task envelope before nested interpretation without writing`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/QUALITY_PLAN.md:25:4. Envelope-version guard — `operation_runner_persistence.ts` — AC4. Reject an unsupported envelope before nested operation interpretation without a write.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:12:- **AC4:** An exact installed candidate run executes the six unique public benchmark tasks with no skips or missing tasks and records the binary SHA, split, and recomputed manifest SHA. Test: `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:63:- **GREEN:** Pinned Bookworm package build completed; after extraction outside the checkout, `node --test eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` passed 3/3 with the actual installed `nexus eval` CLI, runner, and scorer. The rebuilt development artifact is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.1.tar.gz`; it is not exact-commit release evidence.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:64:- **Peer review:** Independent code review returned `APPROVED_WITH_COMMENTS` for AC2. Reviewer confirmed the installed CLI/runner/scorer path and the empty-split file fix; the comment is blocking AC4 evidence, which remains outstanding.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:71:- **Global release-scope guard:** Current `docs/releases/v1.1.2.md` still defines v1.1.2 as a patch on v1.1.1 containing one operation-message fix and inheriting v1.1.1 qualification. `docs/v1.1.0/README.md` also says WP-11xx is not implemented in its described release. This conflicts with the user's direction to complete the full WP-1101..WP-1108 roadmap in v1.1.2. The release definition, integrated branch, qualification and candidate must be reconciled to the full roadmap before any v1.1.2 publication; this WP slice does not change the release notes or release branch.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:72:- **Cross-slice audit (2026-11-02, independent read-only agents):** WP-1101 (`8a83c9e7`) has an unintegrated recorder prototype without runtime event wiring or branch-head gate evidence; WP-1102 (`ee7c8b1e`) has partial redaction work with operator acceptance pending; WP-1103 dataset/runner branches (`e430dab5`, `c548e53e`) have no PR, and required actual provider-request isolation, filesystem/mount denial, post-exit oracle scoring, and six-task G1.1-2 evidence are absent. WP-1105 has no implementation delta, WP-1106 has no branch or implementation, WP-1107 (`9cb5f6de`) is an unintegrated grammar generator prototype without provider-path integration, and WP-1108 (`550112cd`) is a partial modernization policy batch without branch-head gate evidence. None is release-qualified. These are audit leads; revalidate on the integrated exact head before marking any tracker item done.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:78:- AC4 can use the deterministic local fake provider and payload capture specified in `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md`; no public provider is needed for the dataset-isolation acceptance. The release concurrency plan still requires the serial `GATEWAY` claim for evaluator runs. That claim is held by `codex-root` on `ubuntu-desktop` for RC15 E5 provider verification (since 2026-10-31T09:47Z, no PID). This host is `mike-dev`, has a different boot ID, and has no matching process; the claimed worktree remains with untracked RC15 evidence. A handoff/stale determination is not supportable locally, so a conflict/handoff request was appended to the shared claim log and the claim/worktree remain untouched.\n","exit_code":2,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":962498804}},"started_at_ms":1793607668531,"completed_at_ms":1793607669494}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:21:10.916Z","ordinal":34942,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19b59-1c84-72f1-bd8d-3183cc983bec","call_id":"call_062bbcd89d8240d8af24906e906daf8d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 5623)\nTotal output lines: 92\n\n# WP-1104: Standalone `nexus eval` command\n\n## Specification\n\n**User story:** As a Nexus operator, I need to run a versioned evaluation dataset through the installed Nexus executable and receive a structured score file, so that I can compare candidate builds reproducibly without depending on the source checkout.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:**\n\n- **AC1:** `nexus eval --help` exposes `--dataset`, `--split`, `--runs`, `--isolated-home`, and `--output`. Test: `eval CLI help exposes versioned dataset options`.\n- **AC2:** A packaged candidate resolves and executes the installed CLI dispatch, runner, and scorer from its package closure when launched outside the source checkout, without inference for an empty benchmark split. Test: `packaged evaluator runtime executes outside checkout`.\n- **AC3:** A versioned dataset run rejects unsupported `--limit` before creating the output directory or starting the runner; help states that `--limit` applies only to legacy runs. Test: `versioned eval rejects limit before runner or output creation`.\n- **AC4:** An exact installed candidate run executes the six unique public benchmark tasks with no skips or missing tasks and records the binary SHA, split, and recomputed manifest SHA. Test: `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance`.\n- **AC5:** Existing legacy dataset invocation and `--limit` behavior remain compatible. Test: `legacy eval invocation and limit remain supported`.\n\n**Out of scope:** Adding evaluator kinds, changing the public dataset schema, changing legacy scoring, or publishing/tagging a release.\n\n**Dependencies:** WP-1103 versioned dataset and runner foundation at `6adbeb31` and `00a8cb4d` on this branch. WP-1102 is not a functional dependency. WP-1108 is not imported as a branch; package changes will be based on the selected current package script and separately checked against its ownership and gate state.\n\n**Files claimed:** `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`, `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs`, `eval/README.md`, `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs`, `scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md`, and all paths in the accepted WP-1103 commits being integrated.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. **CLI grammar and compatibility** — files: `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`; tests: `eval CLI help exposes versioned dataset options`, `legacy eval invocation and limit remain supported`. Write tests first, verify expected RED, then port the CLI implementation.\n2. **Versioned argument validation** — files: `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`; test: `versioned eval rejects limit before runner or output creation`. Preserve existing runner and filesystem behavior outside this acceptance criterion.\n3. **Versioned runtime dispatch and packaged closure** — files: `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/README.md`, `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs`, `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs`, `scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`; tests: `versioned eval invokes resolved installed runner`, `evaluator runtime allowlist copies only runtime files`, `packaged evaluator runtime executes outside checkout`. First verify resolver/dispatch with a synthetic package; verify the staged allowlist excludes datasets/oracles; then build and stage the actual package and invoke the installed CLI outside the checkout against an empty benchmark split, exercising the real runner and scorer subprocesses without inference. Reconcile package allowlist changes against the current script rather than replaying historical packaging commits.\n4. **Installed candidate acceptance** — files: `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts` and the WP-1103 acceptance evidence path when claimed; test: `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance`. Require six unique manifest IDs, an invocation and validator result for each, zero skips/missing, candidate binary SHA, split, and recomputed manifest SHA.\n\n**Reference corpora:** `nexus-cli` for Commander registration and CLI command dispatch; `nexus-test` for CLI command test patterns; `nexus-wp1104-reference` for the prior WP-1104 resolver and runtime behavior; `nexus-docs` for evaluation acceptance and dataset contracts.\n\n**Risk / unknowns:** The current package script must contain the evaluator closure needed by WP-1105. Retrieval query: \"which evaluator modules are copied into the Linux package and how are runtime paths resolved?\" The installed artifact test is the acceptance gate for this boundary.\n\n## Base and claim state at plan review\n\n- Selected source base: `origin/main` = `593d569b5aa2a43d1b31138d37e90b8b65ffcbe7`.\n- Current package script blob at that base: `5f410376b1c167fa6422ea912d8e69e92ccb8972`.\n- `scripts/package-linux.sh` claim was free before this slice took its claim.\n- WP-1108 triage at `v1/wp-1108-dependency-modernization` says its added CI job has not run at that branch head and its policy batch is not accepted; no WP-1108 packaging changes are treated as a qualified prerequisite.\n- Plan review: approved after narrowing dependencies, adding RED-first named tests, and requiring real package execution outside the checkout.\n\n## Retrieval log\n\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-cli`; query: \"Commander CLI command registration subcommand options action parse\"; hit `index.ts:2`; Commander import and command registration context informed the planned integration seam.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-cli`; definition lookup `createCommand`; MISS. No eval-specific API was derived from this lookup.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-cli`; query: \"registerOperationCommands program.command run resume status options action\"; hit `operation_cli.ts:230`; retrieved the `Command` parameter and chained `.command(...).option(...).action(...)` registration pattern.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-test`; que…2623 tokens truncated…The plan file and `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs` are claimed by root on `v1/v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` at `origin/main` 593d569b. The WP-1103 umbrella claim covers `eval/dataset.mjs`, `eval/datasets/core-v1/**` (public development tasks only), `eval/README.md`, and `docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md`. Runner claims on the same branch cover `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/runner_integrity.mjs`, and `eval/dataset.test.mjs`; that `eval/dataset.test.mjs` claim spans chunks 1 and 2 sequentially. The G1.1-2 evidence is claimed at `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`; write it only after the exact candidate CLI run completes and the final manifest hash is recomputed. Do not edit, index, or expose held-out payloads.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:26:3. **Prove candidate isolation and complete coverage** — use the actual candidate CLI path with a deterministic local fake provider that captures the request after prompt construction. Separately intercept and record the exact `{command, argv, env}` launch payload handed to the sandbox wrapper, and inspect the sandbox payload/stdin at that boundary. Assert the objective appears in the expected argv and captured provider request; the sentinel is absent from serialized argv/environment/stdin; and credentials stay evaluator-side except the intended local proxy token. Keep filesystem/mount checks in the separate `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` test. Score with evaluator-held oracles after candidate exit. Then run every manifest-declared benchmark ID with no skips, recording candidate SHA, dataset/split, recomputed manifest hash, request capture and validator/scorer result in the claimed `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`. Tests/evidence: `versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels`; `candidate launch envelope contains stimulus but no oracle data in argv env or stdin`; `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`; `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`; `versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage`. Requires the installed candidate and package closure from WP-1104; this is the G1.1-2 evidence run, not a unit-test substitute.\ndocs/v1.1.0/QUALITY_PLAN.md:11:- AC4: A future task envelope containing an invalid nested operation reports the envelope-version error before nested interpretation, leaves bytes and mtime unchanged, and creates no backup or quarantine sidecar → test: `replay refuses a future task envelope before nested interpretation without writing`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/QUALITY_PLAN.md:25:4. Envelope-version guard — `operation_runner_persistence.ts` — AC4. Reject an unsupported envelope before nested operation interpretation without a write.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:12:- **AC4:** An exact installed candidate run executes the six unique public benchmark tasks with no skips or missing tasks and records the binary SHA, split, and recomputed manifest SHA. Test: `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance`.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:63:- **GREEN:** Pinned Bookworm package build completed; after extraction outside the checkout, `node --test eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` passed 3/3 with the actual installed `nexus eval` CLI, runner, and scorer. The rebuilt development artifact is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.1.tar.gz`; it is not exact-commit release evidence.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:64:- **Peer review:** Independent code review returned `APPROVED_WITH_COMMENTS` for AC2. Reviewer confirmed the installed CLI/runner/scorer path and the empty-split file fix; the comment is blocking AC4 evidence, which remains outstanding.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:71:- **Global release-scope guard:** Current `docs/releases/v1.1.2.md` still defines v1.1.2 as a patch on v1.1.1 containing one operation-message fix and inheriting v1.1.1 qualification. `docs/v1.1.0/README.md` also says WP-11xx is not implemented in its described release. This conflicts with the user's direction to complete the full WP-1101..WP-1108 roadmap in v1.1.2. The release definition, integrated branch, qualification and candidate must be reconciled to the full roadmap before any v1.1.2 publication; this WP slice does not change the release notes or release branch.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:72:- **Cross-slice audit (2026-11-02, independent read-only agents):** WP-1101 (`8a83c9e7`) has an unintegrated recorder prototype without runtime event wiring or branch-head gate evidence; WP-1102 (`ee7c8b1e`) has partial redaction work with operator acceptance pending; WP-1103 dataset/runner branches (`e430dab5`, `c548e53e`) have no PR, and required actual provider-request isolation, filesystem/mount denial, post-exit oracle scoring, and six-task G1.1-2 evidence are absent. WP-1105 has no implementation delta, WP-1106 has no branch or implementation, WP-1107 (`9cb5f6de`) is an unintegrated grammar generator prototype without provider-path integration, and WP-1108 (`550112cd`) is a partial modernization policy batch without branch-head gate evidence. None is release-qualified. These are audit leads; revalidate on the integrated exact head before marking any tracker item done.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:78:- AC4 can use the deterministic local fake provider and payload capture specified in `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md`; no public provider is needed for the dataset-isolation acceptance. The release concurrency plan still requires the serial `GATEWAY` claim for evaluator runs. That claim is held by `codex-root` on `ubuntu-desktop` for RC15 E5 provider verification (since 2026-10-31T09:47Z, no PID). This host is `mike-dev`, has a different boot ID, and has no matching process; the claimed worktree remains with untracked RC15 evidence. A handoff/stale determination is not supportable locally, so a conflict/handoff request was appended to the shared claim log and the claim/worktree remain untouched.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","create_time":1793607670.9168067}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
