he request after prompt construction. Separately intercept and record the exact `{command, argv, env}` launch payload handed to the sandbox wrapper, and inspect the sandbox payload/stdin at that boundary. Assert the objective appears in the expected argv and captured provider request; the sentinel is absent from serialized argv/environment/stdin; and credentials stay evaluator-side except the intended local proxy token. Keep filesystem/mount checks in the separate `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` test. Score with evaluator-held oracles after candidate exit. Then run every manifest-declared benchmark ID with no skips, recording candidate SHA, dataset/split, recomputed manifest hash, request capture and validator/scorer result in the claimed `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`. Tests/evidence: `versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels`; `candidate launch envelope contains stimulus but no oracle data in argv env or stdin`; `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`; `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`; `versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage`. Requires the installed candidate and package closure from WP-1104; this is the G1.1-2 evidence run, not a unit-test substitute.\n M cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs\n M cli/src/index.ts\n M eval/README.md\n M eval/run.mjs\n M scripts/package-linux.sh\n?? cli/src/eval_cli.ts\n?? cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts\n?? docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md\n?? eval/package_runtime.test.mjs\n?? scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs\n4\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":847404006}},"started_at_ms":1793607721134,"completed_at_ms":1793607721982}}
