{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:22:43.700Z","ordinal":35018,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016ae8485316fc81a3a7dba06736f223eb","status":"completed","call_id":"call_56cb698cfeff4e72a9fb18f3483a3155","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '55,95p' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md; sed -n '1,120p' eval/README.md; cat eval/datasets/core-v1/manifest.json\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:1800});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","create_time":1793607763.0911434}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:22:43.765Z","ordinal":35019,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","session_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","root_turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","response_id":"resp_0fd4138577b17921016ae8484ef9f081a384c4714d1f5c2767","usage":{"input_tokens":92604,"cached_input_tokens":91904,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":576,"reasoning_output_tokens":467,"total_tokens":93180},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":7110441,"cached_input_tokens":6940672,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":20638,"reasoning_output_tokens":4654,"total_tokens":7131079},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":666515385,"cached_input_tokens":660517504,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1419053,"reasoning_output_tokens":728128,"total_tokens":667934438}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:22:46.153Z","ordinal":35020,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3057cfa2-304b-4406-a1ee-cc06e8c15eff","process_id":"2857","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '55,95p' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md; sed -n '1,120p' eval/README.md; cat eval/datasets/core-v1/manifest.json"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '55,95p' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md","name":"WP-1104-PLAN.md","path":"docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,120p' eval/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"eval/README.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat eval/datasets/core-v1/manifest.json","name":"manifest.json","path":"eval/datasets/core-v1/manifest.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## TDD evidence\n\n- **RED:** `eval CLI help exposes versioned dataset options` failed on the expected missing `--dataset` option in the existing CLI help.\n- **RED:** `versioned eval rejects limit before runner or output creation` failed on the expected unrecognized versioned CLI options before the validation was added.\n- **RED:** `versioned eval invokes resolved installed runner` failed because the old legacy evaluator attempted to read the versioned dataset directory as a file (`EISDIR`).\n- **GREEN:** `npm run build` passed; the initial `node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/eval_cli.test.ts` run passed 7/7 with the original empty-dataset legacy case. That test was later strengthened because the initial case did not prove truncation.\n- **RED:** `evaluator runtime allowlist copies only runtime files` failed on the expected empty scaffold allowlist; `evaluator runtime staging fails when an allowlisted module is missing` failed because the scaffold did not validate required files.\n- **RED:** Strengthened `packaged evaluator runtime executes outside checkout` to invoke the packaged CLI and actual runner/scorer against a valid empty dataset; it failed because `eval/run.mjs` did not create `results.jsonl` when the selected split had no tasks.\n- **GREEN:** Pinned Bookworm package build completed; after extraction outside the checkout, `node --test eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` passed 3/3 with the actual installed `nexus eval` CLI, runner, and scorer. The rebuilt development artifact is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.1.tar.gz`; it is not exact-commit release evidence.\n- **Peer review:** Independent code review returned `APPROVED_WITH_COMMENTS` for AC2. Reviewer confirmed the installed CLI/runner/scorer path and the empty-split file fix; the comment is blocking AC4 evidence, which remains outstanding.\n- **AC3 test review:** A second independent read-only review confirmed that passing an invalid `NEXUS_HOME` and asserting the explicit `--limit` diagnostic wins establishes validation-before-runtime-resolution; assertions cover the score parent, score file and artifact directory remaining absent. The focused test has not yet been run because another worktree's test process is still live.\n- **AC5 test review:** An independent read-only review confirmed the non-empty two-task fixture and `--limit 1` assertions exercise real truncation and first-task-only prompting. The reviewer caught that `spawnSync` would block the in-process mock server; the test now uses async `spawn`, which the reviewer confirmed resolves that deadlock. Runtime verification remains pending the shared test lane.\n- **AC5 red/green:** The first strengthened run failed because the mock returned JSON while the client requested SSE (`INFERENCE_FAILED: stream_incomplete`). After switching to the retrieved SSE contract and setting `--workspace` to an isolated empty directory (so evaluator discovery cannot run this repository's test suite), `node cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs test/eval_cli.test.ts` passed 7/7; the non-empty `--limit 1` case confirmed exactly one completion request containing the first prompt and not the second.\n\n## Gate attempt notes\n\n- **Global release-scope guard:** Current `docs/releases/v1.1.2.md` still defines v1.1.2 as a patch on v1.1.1 containing one operation-message fix and inheriting v1.1.1 qualification. `docs/v1.1.0/README.md` also says WP-11xx is not implemented in its described release. This conflicts with the user's direction to complete the full WP-1101..WP-1108 roadmap in v1.1.2. The release definition, integrated branch, qualification and candidate must be reconciled to the full roadmap before any v1.1.2 publication; this WP slice does not change the release notes or release branch.\n- **Cross-slice audit (2026-11-02, independent read-only agents):** WP-1101 (`8a83c9e7`) has an unintegrated recorder prototype without runtime event wiring or branch-head gate evidence; WP-1102 (`ee7c8b1e`) has partial redaction work with operator acceptance pending; WP-1103 dataset/runner branches (`e430dab5`, `c548e53e`) have no PR, and required actual provider-request isolation, filesystem/mount denial, post-exit oracle scoring, and six-task G1.1-2 evidence are absent. WP-1105 has no implementation delta, WP-1106 has no branch or implementation, WP-1107 (`9cb5f6de`) is an unintegrated grammar generator prototype without provider-path integration, and WP-1108 (`550112cd`) is a partial modernization policy batch without branch-head gate evidence. None is release-qualified. These are audit leads; revalidate on the integrated exact head before marking any tracker item done.\n\n- A first `npm test` run on `/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-suite-snapshot` was diagnostic only: the snapshot had no `cli/dist/index.js` or Rust core binaries, and `NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT` was unset so the actual package smoke was skipped. Its test runner reported 1,981 tests (1,739 pass, 222 fail) and then remained in `turn_semantics.test.ts` with repeated provider-recovery retries; that process was interrupted after about 40 minutes. This is not accepted full-suite evidence.\n- Snapshot prerequisites are now built: `npm run build` and debug `cargo build --locked --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui` passed. Release core binaries were copied from the successful pinned Bookworm package build, whose Rust sources are unchanged by this WP-1104 slice.\n- A separate focused test process in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/pr398-review` remains active. The next full-suite attempt must wait for it to finish, then set `NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT` to the freshly extracted development package so the actual outside-checkout runtime test runs instead of skipping.\n- After peer review identified that the former empty-dataset `--limit 0` case did not prove truncation, the legacy compatibility test was strengthened to a non-empty two-task fixture and async local OpenAI-compatible mock. The first mock response format caused an expected transport failure; the second run timed out because the evaluator used the repository as its workspace and discovered the repository test command. Both causes were corrected. Current targeted TypeScript no-emit and `git diff --check` pass, and the updated focused suite passes 7/7.\n- AC4 can use the deterministic local fake provider and payload capture specified in `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md`; no public provider is needed for the dataset-isolation acceptance. The release concurrency plan still requires the serial `GATEWAY` claim for evaluator runs. That claim is held by `codex-root` on `ubuntu-desktop` for RC15 E5 provider verification (since 2026-10-31T09:47Z, no PID). This host is `mike-dev`, has a different boot ID, and has no matching process; the claimed worktree remains with untracked RC15 evidence. A handoff/stale determination is not supportable locally, so a conflict/handoff request was appended to the shared claim log and the claim/worktree remain untouched.\n# Evaluation harness (qualification assessment §9)\n\n`run.mjs` runs tasks against one agent configuration and appends a JSON line per run; `score.mjs` reports the scores\nseparately (never combined), per task and configuration, with 95 % Wilson intervals.\n\n`docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md` is a historical checkpoint at source revision `6151a23`; use this file and the current\nrunner source for evaluator behavior added after that revision. Neither document represents completed M5 qualification.\n\n```bash\nnode eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/gateway-engineering-deep.json --out eval/out/<label> [--only id,id] [--runs N]\nnode eval/score.mjs eval/out/<label>/results.jsonl          # markdown table; --json for machine output\nnode eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$NEXUS_RESULTS\" \"$GOOSE_RESULTS\" \"$OPENCODE_RESULTS\"\n```\n\n## Installed versioned datasets\n\nInstalled releases expose the versioned runner through the Nexus CLI:\n\n```bash\nnexus eval --dataset /path/to/core-v1 --split benchmark --runs 1 \\\n  --isolated-home --output ./results/benchmark.json\n```\n\nThe dataset path must be a versioned dataset directory. The installed command loads its runner from the package named by\n`NEXUS_HOME`; it does not fall back to evaluator code in a development checkout. The score file is created with\nowner-only permissions, and per-task run artifacts are written beside it under `<output>.artifacts`. The legacy\n`nexus eval <dataset-file> --limit N` form remains available for file-based benchmark datasets. `--limit` is not\nsupported for versioned dataset directories; select `--split` or provide a dataset containing the desired task set.\n\nEach run uses a frozen copy of the task tree, a fresh workspace and `HOME`, and a unique output directory. The agent\nreceives only its workspace, isolated home, selected read-only runtime files, and a run-scoped token for a local proxy;\nthe real gateway credential stays in the harness process. The candidate runs in Bubblewrap user, PID and network\nnamespaces, with nested user namespaces disabled. Legacy development tasks may still use `hidden: { dir, into, command }`;\nthose commands execute against the candidate workspace after the agent exits and are **not safe for qualification**, because\nvalidator code can inspect or modify files in that workspace. Qualification requires `hidden: { protocol: \"blackbox-v1\",\ncasesFile, runtime, argv, timeoutMs, totalTimeoutMs, maxOutputBytes }`. Its private JSON cases contain only `input` and\n`expected`; the host evaluator keeps expected values in its process and launches the candidate runtime separately for each\ninput using a fresh top-level Bubblewrap boundary. The candidate receives one input on stdin and returns one JSON value on\nstdout. Its workspace is read-only; private oracle files are not mounted. Candidate output and diagnostics are discarded,\nand result logs contain only case counts and failed indexes. Supported runtimes are explicitly allowlisted (`node`,\n`python3`); the only argument is a validated relative candidate entrypoint (no runtime flags, eval expressions, or extra\narguments), and per-case/aggregate time and output bounds are enforced. Oracle files must be outside the copied fixture.\nAbsolute paths, traversal, symlinks and unsupported fixture entries are rejected. `manifest.json` records the harness source-file hashes, model fingerprint, corpus/task\nhashes when qualification is configured, executable version, budgets, host and Node version. Each result records the\nexecutable version and effective step/minute budget; per-run logs go to `logs/<task>-<run>/`. The runner refuses an\nexisting output directory so a retry cannot append to or replace prior evidence.\n\nQualification runs require `nexusExecutable` to name the absolute path of the installed RC,\n`expectedAgentVersion` to pin its version, and `nexusPackageSha256` to record the expected release-asset digest from checksum verification. The runner checks `nexus --version` and refuses the checkout\n`cli/dist/index.js` or a version mismatch before starting an agent. Peer versions are read using each adapter's\n`--version` command inside the same Bubblewrap filesystem/network boundary, with a cleared environment and bounded\noutput/time; executable paths and SHA-256 hashes are archived alongside the RC package\ndigest. `score.mjs --pairs` takes exactly the Nexus,\nGoose and OpenCode result files and refuses mismatched model fingerprints, sampling declarations, context/output\nlimits, explicit per-task request and aggregate requested-output ceilings, run pairs, executable identities, or\neffective step/minute budgets. The proxy permits only model-catalog and inference routes, strips client-supplied\nauthorization and control-plane headers, and enforces configured request/body/output ceilings. These are requested\ncompletion-token ceilings, not exact usage accounting. It reports peer hidden-test results\nseparately; scores are never combined. The Nexus adapter passes the recorded temperature and step/minute limits;\nOpenCode receives a primary evaluation agent with the recorded step limit, temperature and seed; Goose receives the\nmatching `--max-turns`, context/output limits and temperature settings. Qualification mode currently requires\n`sampling.temperature` to be `0` across all three adapters; seed metadata remains recorded when configured.\n\n## Task format (`eval/tasks/<id>/task.json`)\n\nThe versioned dataset loader and installed `nexus eval --dataset ... --split ...` command support governed task populations. The CLI dispatches the packaged runner against a versioned dataset directory, while `eval/run.mjs` continues to accept the legacy task directory. Each dataset contains\n`manifest.json`, `examples.jsonl`, `oracles.jsonl`, and `tasks/<id>/`. The manifest pins SHA-256 digests of both JSONL\nfiles and exact split counts. `examples.jsonl` has an allowlisted stimulus schema (`id`, `split`, `domain`, `objective`,\n`taskDir`, and optional task budgets/classification); it cannot contain oracle fields. `oracles.jsonl` has the same unique\nIDs and evaluator-only `hidden` and `regression` records. The loader rejects digest mismatch, duplicate/missing IDs,\nunknown fields, unsupported splits, count mismatch, path escape, and symlinks. The loader keeps oracle records separate from\nstimulus records; the versioned runner stages fixtures and applies its Bubblewrap namespace and mount policies. Full WP-1103 provider-request and filesystem-isolation acceptance remains a separate qualification gate. Dataset task\ndirectories keep a sanitized `task.json` with fixture metadata and no objective or oracle commands. `eval/tasks/` remains\navailable as a legacy input while datasets and configs migrate. Loader bounds are 64 KiB per manifest, 32 MiB per JSONL\nfile, 1 MiB per record, 10,000 records, and 50,000 task-tree entries (maximum depth 64, 64 MiB per file, 512 MiB per\ntask tree).\n\nThe committed `eval/datasets/core-v1/` is the first migrated population: one regression self-test and six benchmark\ntasks. It can be run through the installed CLI with `nexus eval --dataset eval/datasets/core-v1 --split benchmark`. Held-out qualification corpora remain under their separately approved custody process and are not copied into\nthis public development dataset.\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `id`, `tier` | T1 smoke (scripted model, CI), T2 standard, T3 long-task, T4 fault-injected |\n| `fixture` or `repo` | a directory in the task, or `{ \"url\", \"commit\" }` (external repositories at pinned commits) |\n| `setup` | shell commands run in the workspace before the agent (e.g. `npm ci`) |\n| `objective` | the operator text given to the agent |\n| `steps`, `minutes` | budgets (defaults from the configuration: 300 steps, 120 min) |\n| `hidden` | `{ dir, into, command, timeoutSec }` — tests the agent never sees; pass = artifact correct |\n| `regression` | `{ command }` — the repository's own suite after the run |\n\n## Scores\n\ncompletion claimed · artifact correct (hidden tests) · false VERIFIED (VERIFIED while hidden tests fail) · regressions\nintroduced · timed out / harness errors · wall time, steps, tokens (median). Context qualifier (`contextNotRetained`) is\nrecorded per run.\n\n## Scoring integrity\n\n- **Model proxy.** Every agent reaches the model through a per-run forwarder (`eval/model_proxy.mjs`) that `run.mjs`\n  starts. Each record carries `model: { requests, answered, upstreamFailures, firstRequestAt, firstAnswerAt }`. Set\n  `\"proxy\": false` in a config to connect agents directly; such runs are then scored only by the legacy rule below.\n- **Infrastructure reruns** (`eval/infra.mjs`). A run is rerun only when the model never answered *and* the endpoint\n  was observed failing, or when the harness itself errored. The rule is the same for every agent. A run in which the\n  model answered is always scored: a crash is a failure (and counts towards the crash rate), not a rerun. Records from\n  before the proxy fall back to each agent's own connection-failure message, and the script says how many it judged\n  that way.\n- **Contamination.** Contaminated runs (the task directory changed, or its path appeared in the agent's output) are\n  left out of pooled pass rates and counted separately.\n- **Reruns are listed.** `score.mjs` lists every replaced run with what it showed and what the rerun showed.\n- **Pooled metrics.** Pooled rows report crash rate, regressions, tokens per correct result and wall seconds per\n  correct result. The cost of failed runs counts towards these.\n\n## Fault injection (T4)\n\nA task or config may list `faults: [{ kind, atRequest }]`. The run's model proxy then injects that fault into the Nth\nchat request (counted from 1):\n\n| kind | Fault |\n|---|---|\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"name\": \"core-v1\",\n  \"version\": \"1.1.0\",\n  \"description\": \"Versioned development and benchmark tasks migrated from eval/tasks.\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"splits\": {\n    \"regression\": {\n      \"count\": 1\n    },\n    \"benchmark\": {\n      \"count\": 6\n    }\n  },\n  \"domains\": [\n    \"harness-integrity\",\n    \"coding-task\"\n  ],\n  \"files\": {\n    \"examples.jsonl\": \"b16cbc374ddbadf9f652b2eea5336b428da1c5ff6e0badfe654f2e85789a4018\",\n    \"oracles.jsonl\": \"d5109d77b4d38fc99d318505a3336604c74059f2e4cf28fc383113e46fd28516\"\n  },\n  \"tasks\": {\n    \"selftest-add\": \"44759ecf54855bca4487eb4a5bd3b110ada1f74b3639b17e7aae64957a9759cf\",\n    \"t2-bugfix-csv\": \"6a1ed7beb4b4b5f1fe4326795648f64f47a90a814f63157d1b69e9c706917fa8\",\n    \"t2-bugfix-duration\": \"8529090965b72eff940cf1545943295730a0fbf60e92cea5438a49c1f140b696\",\n    \"t2-debug-logs\": \"440e635553fdfd39508bb565e3664063b6688ce8f9a1c7b366cab4446a9087d4\",\n    \"t2-feature-inventory\": \"fc706e7cf98b47e9a17d00717aa00262a734e165352e2fc489e853dcc59ffd46\",\n    \"t2-feature-slugify\": \"a187297977130bf7c4dcf0bf7956297ae380c2ae402a25b85482c34067dc6301\",\n    \"t2-refactor-tax\": \"e94cbd1fd2c787e09425ffd6141b8e333ba8dadea08509a0ab0b685e83aa42ad\"\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":58617300}},"started_at_ms":1793607765092,"completed_at_ms":1793607766152}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:22:49.568Z","ordinal":35021,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19b5a-9de0-7321-8111-00e39685e915","call_id":"call_56cb698cfeff4e72a9fb18f3483a3155","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 5.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 4465)\nTotal output lines: 176\n\n## TDD evidence\n\n- **RED:** `eval CLI help exposes versioned dataset options` failed on the expected missing `--dataset` option in the existing CLI help.\n- **RED:** `versioned eval rejects limit before runner or output creation` failed on the expected unrecognized versioned CLI options before the validation was added.\n- **RED:** `versioned eval invokes resolved installed runner` failed because the old legacy evaluator attempted to read the versioned dataset directory as a file (`EISDIR`).\n- **GREEN:** `npm run build` passed; the initial `node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/eval_cli.test.ts` run passed 7/7 with the original empty-dataset legacy case. That test was later strengthened because the initial case did not prove truncation.\n- **RED:** `evaluator runtime allowlist copies only runtime files` failed on the expected empty scaffold allowlist; `evaluator runtime staging fails when an allowlisted module is missing` failed because the scaffold did not validate required files.\n- **RED:** Strengthened `packaged evaluator runtime executes outside checkout` to invoke the packaged CLI and actual runner/scorer against a valid empty dataset; it failed because `eval/run.mjs` did not create `results.jsonl` when the selected split had no tasks.\n- **GREEN:** Pinned Bookworm package build completed; after extraction outside the checkout, `node --test eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` passed 3/3 with the actual installed `nexus eval` CLI, runner, and scorer. The rebuilt development artifact is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.1.tar.gz`; it is not exact-commit release evidence.\n- **Peer review:** Independent code review returned `APPROVED_WITH_COMMENTS` for AC2. Reviewer confirmed the installed CLI/runner/scorer path and the empty-split file fix; the comment is blocking AC4 evidence, which remains outstanding.\n- **AC3 test review:** A second independent read-only review confirmed that passing an invalid `NEXUS_HOME` and asserting the explicit `--limit` diagnostic wins establishes validation-before-runtime-resolution; assertions cover the score parent, score file and artifact directory remaining absent. The focused test has not yet been run because another worktree's test process is still live.\n- **AC5 test review:** An independent read-only review confirmed the non-empty two-task fixture and `--limit 1` assertions exercise real truncation and first-task-only prompting. The reviewer caught that `spawnSync` would block the in-process mock server; the test now uses async `spawn`, which the reviewer confirmed resolves that deadlock. Runtime verification remains pending the shared test lane.\n- **AC5 red/green:** The first strengthened run failed because the mock returned JSON while the client requested SSE (`INFERENCE_FAILED: stream_incomplete`). After switching to the retrieved SSE contract and setting `--workspace` to an isolated empty directory (so evaluator discovery cannot run this repository's test suite), `node cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs test/eval_cli.test.ts` passed 7/7; the non-empty `--limit 1` case confirmed exactly one completion request containing the first prompt and not the second.\n\n## Gate attempt notes\n\n- **Global release-scope guard:** Current `docs/releases/v1.1.2.md` still defines v1.1.2 as a patch on v1.1.1 containing one operation-message fix and inheriting v1.1.1 qualification. `docs/v1.1.0/README.md` also says WP-11xx is not implemented in its described release. This conflicts with the user's direction to complete the full WP-1101..WP-1108 roadmap in v1.1.2. The release definition, integrated branch, qualification and candidate must be reco…2665 tokens truncated…ipted model, CI), T2 standard, T3 long-task, T4 fault-injected |\n| `fixture` or `repo` | a directory in the task, or `{ \"url\", \"commit\" }` (external repositories at pinned commits) |\n| `setup` | shell commands run in the workspace before the agent (e.g. `npm ci`) |\n| `objective` | the operator text given to the agent |\n| `steps`, `minutes` | budgets (defaults from the configuration: 300 steps, 120 min) |\n| `hidden` | `{ dir, into, command, timeoutSec }` — tests the agent never sees; pass = artifact correct |\n| `regression` | `{ command }` — the repository's own suite after the run |\n\n## Scores\n\ncompletion claimed · artifact correct (hidden tests) · false VERIFIED (VERIFIED while hidden tests fail) · regressions\nintroduced · timed out / harness errors · wall time, steps, tokens (median). Context qualifier (`contextNotRetained`) is\nrecorded per run.\n\n## Scoring integrity\n\n- **Model proxy.** Every agent reaches the model through a per-run forwarder (`eval/model_proxy.mjs`) that `run.mjs`\n  starts. Each record carries `model: { requests, answered, upstreamFailures, firstRequestAt, firstAnswerAt }`. Set\n  `\"proxy\": false` in a config to connect agents directly; such runs are then scored only by the legacy rule below.\n- **Infrastructure reruns** (`eval/infra.mjs`). A run is rerun only when the model never answered *and* the endpoint\n  was observed failing, or when the harness itself errored. The rule is the same for every agent. A run in which the\n  model answered is always scored: a crash is a failure (and counts towards the crash rate), not a rerun. Records from\n  before the proxy fall back to each agent's own connection-failure message, and the script says how many it judged\n  that way.\n- **Contamination.** Contaminated runs (the task directory changed, or its path appeared in the agent's output) are\n  left out of pooled pass rates and counted separately.\n- **Reruns are listed.** `score.mjs` lists every replaced run with what it showed and what the rerun showed.\n- **Pooled metrics.** Pooled rows report crash rate, regressions, tokens per correct result and wall seconds per\n  correct result. The cost of failed runs counts towards these.\n\n## Fault injection (T4)\n\nA task or config may list `faults: [{ kind, atRequest }]`. The run's model proxy then injects that fault into the Nth\nchat request (counted from 1):\n\n| kind | Fault |\n|---|---|\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"name\": \"core-v1\",\n  \"version\": \"1.1.0\",\n  \"description\": \"Versioned development and benchmark tasks migrated from eval/tasks.\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-31T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"splits\": {\n    \"regression\": {\n      \"count\": 1\n    },\n    \"benchmark\": {\n      \"count\": 6\n    }\n  },\n  \"domains\": [\n    \"harness-integrity\",\n    \"coding-task\"\n  ],\n  \"files\": {\n    \"examples.jsonl\": \"b16cbc374ddbadf9f652b2eea5336b428da1c5ff6e0badfe654f2e85789a4018\",\n    \"oracles.jsonl\": \"d5109d77b4d38fc99d318505a3336604c74059f2e4cf28fc383113e46fd28516\"\n  },\n  \"tasks\": {\n    \"selftest-add\": \"44759ecf54855bca4487eb4a5bd3b110ada1f74b3639b17e7aae64957a9759cf\",\n    \"t2-bugfix-csv\": \"6a1ed7beb4b4b5f1fe4326795648f64f47a90a814f63157d1b69e9c706917fa8\",\n    \"t2-bugfix-duration\": \"8529090965b72eff940cf1545943295730a0fbf60e92cea5438a49c1f140b696\",\n    \"t2-debug-logs\": \"440e635553fdfd39508bb565e3664063b6688ce8f9a1c7b366cab4446a9087d4\",\n    \"t2-feature-inventory\": \"fc706e7cf98b47e9a17d00717aa00262a734e165352e2fc489e853dcc59ffd46\",\n    \"t2-feature-slugify\": \"a187297977130bf7c4dcf0bf7956297ae380c2ae402a25b85482c34067dc6301\",\n    \"t2-refactor-tax\": \"e94cbd1fd2c787e09425ffd6141b8e333ba8dadea08509a0ab0b685e83aa42ad\"\n  }\n}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","create_time":1793607769.5681334}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_ove