{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T10:03:01.928Z","ordinal":37815,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016ae85fd052f081a3bec9ccb95759867c","status":"completed","call_id":"call_f314afa3072945f9b81fa1d6ccd238de","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md\\n@@\\n - **Cross-slice audit (2026-11-02, independent read-only agents):** WP-1101 (`8a83c9e7`) has an unintegrated recorder prototype without runtime event wiring or branch-head gate evidence; WP-1102 (`ee7c8b1e`) has partial redaction work with operator acceptance pending; WP-1103 dataset/runner branches (`e430dab5`, `c548e53e`) have no PR, and required actual provider-request isolation, filesystem/mount denial, post-exit oracle scoring, and six-task G1.1-2 evidence are absent. WP-1105 has no implementation delta, WP-1106 has no branch or implementation, WP-1107 (`9cb5f6de`) is an unintegrated grammar generator prototype without provider-path integration, and WP-1108 (`550112cd`) is a partial modernization policy batch without branch-head gate evidence. None is release-qualified. These are audit leads; revalidate on the integrated exact head before marking any tracker item done.\\n+\\n+## Gate update — 2026-11-02\\n+\\n+The notes above describe intermediate attempts and are superseded where they conflict with this gate update. After correcting the relative hidden-command checks and making evidence creation exclusive and candidate-specific, independent review by `/root/review_delta` returned **APPROVED** for the WP-1103/1104 source and six-task evidence. The reviewer did not rerun tests.\\n+\\n+The final synchronized full-suite run completed with **2,138 tests, 2,136 passed, 0 failed, and 2 skipped**. The terminal process-scope postcheck reported `scope measurement fixtures passed`. Log: `/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-suite-snapshot/wp1104-suite-final-ac4.log`; SHA-256: `19aeb576f3be4f45b7507d79a0a1cfda1a46e9caebca59f87de9e60b17bf5a16`. The modified source and test files were byte-for-byte matched against the suite snapshot. `npm run build` passed on the integration worktree. The full-suite and process-scope claim was released after all test processes exited.\\n+\\n+Installed-candidate evidence is recorded in `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-b385cd533f9e-suite.json` for package archive SHA-256 `b385cd533f9e14bb161dba9a352d310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a`. It records all six benchmark tasks and captured requests, with no missing or skipped task. The loopback deterministic provider does not establish model quality: its task-completion responses are not solutions, and hidden checks are recorded false. This is dataset execution and request-isolation evidence only. Per the 2026-11-02 coordinator ruling, this mock-only acceptance does not consume the GATEWAY claim; any remote/provider-backed inference still requires that claim.\\n+\\n+This gate closes the WP-1103/1104 source slice only. It does not qualify a tagged release artifact or satisfy the full WP-1101..WP-1108 roadmap. `docs/releases/v1.1.2.md` still describes a narrower patch and must be reconciled with the user's full-roadmap scope before publication. The built archive predates the source commit and does not carry an explicit source-commit binding; it is not exact-commit release evidence.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19b9f-f23a-70e0-bbf9-0adf509bb26d","create_time":1793613776.3250954}}}
