{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T10:16:19.188Z","ordinal":38399,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a19bc2-85f3-7751-ba1f-01be7256c4ab","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Current: 2026-11-02 10:16am UTC\nThis file has prior observations — supplementary context follows. The Read result below is the full requested section.\n- **Need details on a past observation?** get_observations([IDs]) — ~300 tokens each.\n- **Need a structural map first?** smart_outline(\"docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md\") — line numbers only, cheaper than re-reading.\n### Nov 2, 2026\n27279 10:09a 🔵 WP-1103 Acceptance Evidence Uses Prohibited Prior Manifest SHA — AC5 Evidence File Must Be Regenerated"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19b9f-f23a-70e0-bbf9-0adf509bb26d","create_time":1793614579.1878822,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T10:16:20.192Z","ordinal":38400,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19b9f-f23a-70e0-bbf9-0adf509bb26d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ed07d99f-927d-48ea-abde-dc2d773fa9d8","process_id":"45570","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","tail -n 45 docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"tail -n 45 docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md","name":"WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md","path":"docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# WP-1103: Versioned Dataset Oracle Isolation\n\n## Specification\n\n**User story:** As an evaluation operator, I need versioned datasets to keep task stimulus separate from evaluator assertions, so that benchmark results cannot be inflated by exposing expected answers to the candidate.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:**\n\n- **AC1:** For a selected versioned example, the objective reaches the actual candidate prompt/provider-request boundary, while synthetic oracle-only assertion/validator sentinels are absent from the candidate prompt, request, argv, environment, stdin, and other candidate-visible input channels. Tests: `versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels`; `candidate launch envelope contains stimulus but no oracle data in argv env or stdin`.\n- **AC2:** The candidate's staged workspace and declared filesystem/mount view expose the task fixture repository but do not expose the dataset task directory or hidden validator files by path or content. Test: `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`.\n- **AC3:** Dataset selection returns exactly the manifest-declared IDs for the requested `regression` or `benchmark` split and rejects unknown/empty splits or task IDs. Tests: `dataset selection returns exactly manifest-declared ids for each split`; `dataset selection refuses unknown ids and invalid splits`.\n- **AC3a:** Loading rejects changes to oracle records or task-tree content after manifest freeze. Tests: `loader rejects oracle data changed after its manifest was frozen`; `loader rejects task data changed after its manifest was frozen`.\n- **AC4:** After the candidate exits, the evaluator can still access the private oracle record and produce the expected score for the synthetic fixture. Test: `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`.\n- **AC5:** Run the exact candidate CLI against a local fake provider that captures the actual request after prompt construction; record one candidate invocation and validator/scorer result for each of the six manifest-declared benchmark task IDs, with zero skipped or missing tasks. Pin the candidate SHA, dataset version/split, and the SHA-256 recomputed from the final integrated `core-v1/manifest.json`; do not reuse the prior branch's `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43` as current evidence. Test/evidence: `versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage`. This establishes execution coverage and request isolation, not model quality.\n\n**Out of scope:** Modifying oracle semantics, held-out corpus data or custody; changing evaluator scoring; packaging the runtime; live inference against a real model/provider. AC5 uses the actual candidate CLI and prompt path with a local deterministic fake provider; the fake provider captures the request and returns a fixture response so the evaluator can score every declared benchmark task.\n\n**Dependencies:** WP-1103 versioned dataset loader and runner integration; current runner claims are held by root after the prior claim was recorded stale and broken; a test seam for AC1, AC2 and AC4. AC5 requires an integrated exact-candidate benchmark run and is separate from the unit regression suite; packaged installed CLI behavior depends on WP-1104.\n\n**Files claimed/current ownership:** The plan file and `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs` are claimed by root on `v1/v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` at `origin/main` 593d569b. The WP-1103 umbrella claim covers `eval/dataset.mjs`, `eval/datasets/core-v1/**` (public development tasks only), `eval/README.md`, and `docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md`. Runner claims on the same branch cover `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/runner_integrity.mjs`, and `eval/dataset.test.mjs`; that `eval/dataset.test.mjs` claim spans chunks 1 and 2 sequentially. The G1.1-2 evidence is claimed at `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`; write it only after the exact candidate CLI run completes and the final manifest hash is recomputed. Do not edit, index, or expose held-out payloads.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. **Reconcile the versioned dataset** — on `origin/main` 593d569b, add tests first for manifest digest/version validation, split selection, task ID rejection, and task/oracle separation; then port the public `core-v1` dataset loader, examples/oracles, task fixtures and docs. Files: `eval/dataset.mjs`, `eval/datasets/core-v1/**`, `eval/dataset.test.mjs`, `eval/README.md`, `docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md`, `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs`. Tests: `dataset selection returns exactly manifest-declared ids for each split`; `dataset selection refuses unknown ids and invalid splits`; `loader rejects stimulus data changed after its manifest was frozen`; `loader rejects oracle data changed after its manifest was frozen`; `loader rejects task data changed after its manifest was frozen` in `eval/dataset.test.mjs`.\n2. **Wire and harden the runner** — author failing regressions first for bounded task snapshots, explicit installed executable identity, private config/key files, safe output directory, and post-exit scoring; then implement the runner integrity guard and importable versioned API and integrate it with `eval/run.mjs`. Files: `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/runner_integrity.mjs`, `eval/dataset.test.mjs`. Tests: `per-run versioned snapshot guard preserves the bounded dataset digest`; `importable runner API passes only evaluator config and keeps credentials private`; `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`. Keep the `eval/dataset.test.mjs` claim held across chunks 1 and 2.\n3. **Prove candidate isolation and complete coverage** — use the actual candidate CLI path with a deterministic local fake provider that captures the request after prompt construction. Separately intercept and record the exact `{command, argv, env}` launch payload handed to the sandbox wrapper, and inspect the sandbox payload/stdin at that boundary. Assert the objective appears in the expected argv and captured provider request; the sentinel is absent from serialized argv/environment/stdin; and credentials stay evaluator-side except the intended local proxy token. Keep filesystem/mount checks in the separate `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` test. Score with evaluator-held oracles after candidate exit. Then run every manifest-declared benchmark ID with no skips, recording candidate SHA, dataset/split, recomputed manifest hash, request capture and validator/scorer result in the claimed `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`. Tests/evidence: `versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels`; `candidate launch envelope contains stimulus but no oracle data in argv env or stdin`; `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`; `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`; `versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage`. Requires the installed candidate and package closure from WP-1104; this is the G1.1-2 evidence run, not a unit-test substitute.\n4. **Run gates on the integrated head** — run evaluator focused tests, TypeScript build/type gate, exact project test suite, process-scope gate, and package/installed qualification on a free `SUITE`; tie every result to the final exact commit and manifest SHA.\n\n**Reference corpora:** `nexus-test` for existing CLI test conventions; `nexus-cli` for subprocess boundary and agent invocation patterns.\n\n**Retrieved references:** `nexus-test` `eval_harness.test.ts:185-211` uses a fake executable on `PATH` and captures spawned arguments/logs without a live provider; `nexus-test` `harness.test.ts:875` exercises refusal before inference. These are test-seam precedents, not proof of the Nexus runner's exact provider request or filesystem mount boundary. XERJ query: `capture spawned child process command arguments in tests without live provider`; second query: `spawnSync mock executable capture process argv and environment in test`.\n\n**Retrieval log (runner API chunk):** `2026-11-02T00:34Z` — corpus `nexus-test`, query `capture spawned child process arguments environment and stdin in tests without live provider`, hit `eval_integrity.test.ts:1220`; contract: test marker paths are passed as argv rather than interpolated into child source, used as a subprocess-test precedent. `2026-11-02T00:34Z` — corpus `nexus-cli`, definition query `agentCommand`, `MISS`; this symbol is local to `eval/run.mjs` and absent from the indexed CLI source, so the adapter was extracted from the current harness implementation and locked by a failing test before the edit.\n\n**Risk / unknown:** The current runner merges example and oracle fields into an evaluator-side task record before launching the candidate. The exact prompt/provider request and candidate filesystem/mount boundary must be observed without a live model; the fake provider/request capture must establish the actual CLI prompt path, and filesystem checks must establish access denial rather than mere omission from the staged copy. The benchmark evidence must identify the exact candidate SHA, dataset version, split, manifest SHA-256, denominator and each task invocation/result.\n\n**Coordination:** The original plan was independently approved by `review_delta` and `release_gate_audit`. The previous runner claim was older than 24 hours, its clean branch was still `c548e53e`, the host had rebooted since the claim, and no process had its worktree as cwd; `.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log` records the stale-claim break at 2026-11-01T21:56Z. Old dataset and runner branches are preserved as read-only reference. Fresh claims now point to `v1/v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` at `origin/main` 593d569b. Re-review this updated plan before coding. The previous SUITE claim was released after host reboot interrupted its run; claim SUITE before the next suite.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":827430693}},"started_at_ms":1793614579364,"completed_at_ms":1793614580192}}
