{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T10:32:53.968Z","ordinal":38812,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a19bd1-b3d0-7603-bdfa-8a32af01c9c4","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Deliverables: write a deck, report, page or other file the person asked for as a file and attach it as work_product before you finish. When you stop, claude-mem copies each attached file (and any deck, document, page, image or spreadsheet you wrote outside the source tree) into this project's deliverables bucket, ~/.claude-mem/deliverables/<project>/, and links it on the request's card in My Work.\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- v1.1.2-release: state=WP-1104 standalone eval slice is closed with commits 05c49df2 and 2a94f62e, final full suite/build green, peer review approved, and WP-1104-only claims released. Full v1.1.2 roadmap/release remains active., phase=GREEN, gate=WP-1103 AC2 focused dataset test PASS (3/3); fresh full npm test plus process-scope postcheck running in suite snapshot under SUITE claim; new unique candidate evidence path claimed, next=Monitor run 8783 to completion, verify full suite totals, scope postcheck and evidence hashes, then obtain independent review and reconcile WP-1103 claims., friction=WP-1103 earlier review identified AC2 lacked dataset-specific absolute-path/mount-view proof; supplemental test now verifies /workspace mount present, dataset root absent, and absolute hidden validator unreadable. WP-1103 claim ownership metadata still references old runner-reclaim worktree; reconcile before closure., updated=2026-11-02T10:19:00Z, reviewer=/root/review_delta, verdict=APPROVED for 05c49df2 and 2a94f62e, retrieval=nexus-test eval_integrity.test.ts:1729 SSE tool-call stream; eval_harness.test.ts:43 deterministic reply pattern; provider_connect.test.ts:31 local provider harness, updated 14 minutes ago\n- ...783 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-11-02 10:32am UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 25 obs (10,393t read) | 50,217t work | 79% savings\n\n### Nov 2, 2026\n27290 10:12a ○ sandbox.ts Bubblewrap Read-Only Host Confinement: fd-Pinned Workspace Bind\n27291 \" ○ tools.ts Read-Only Mode: Workspace Identity Check Before Command Execution\n27292 10:13a ○ eval/runner_api.mjs: Agent Launched Inside /workspace with sandboxRuntimeRoots Validation\n27293 \" ○ eval/run.mjs Import Map: Full Eval Pipeline Module Dependencies\n27294 \" ○ eval/run.mjs: Agent Launch via serializeAgentLaunchPayload with Output Bounds and T3 Protocol Driver\n27295 \" ○ eval/run.mjs: Multi-Agent Support — nexus, aider, opencode Launch Configurations\n27296 \" ○ eval/isolate.mjs: Two Sandbox Argv Builders — agentSandboxArgv vs isolatedProcessArgv\n27297 \" ○ eval/isolate.mjs agentSandboxArgv: Hardened Bwrap Namespace with Fixed Mount Layout\n27298 \" ○ agentSandboxArgv: Five Sequential Safety Gates Before Bwrap Namespace Creation\n27299 \" ○ agentSandboxArgv: Full Bwrap Namespace Flags — User+PID+Net Unshared, Die-With-Parent\n27300 10:15a ◆ eval_dataset.test.ts: Mount Boundary Probe Added for WP-1103 AC2 Sandbox Isolation\n27301 \" ● eval_dataset.test.ts Mount Probe: Test Fails Due to doesNotMatch on Actual Tool Result String Containing Probe Command Text\n27302 \" ● eval_dataset.test.ts: Mount Probe Assertions Fixed — Scope to stdout Only\n27303 10:16a ● eval_dataset.test.ts Mount Probe: All 3 Tests Now Pass After Assertion Fix\n27304 \" ○ WP-1103 AC2 Definition: Workspace Isolation Must Show Access Denial, Not Mere Omission\n27305 \" ✓ WP-1103 Oracle Isolation Plan: AC2 Addendum Added Documenting Mount View Probe\n27306 \" ✓ Work State Updated: WP-1103 AC2 Mount Probe Complete, Awaiting Plan Review\n27309 10:18a ○ Suite Snapshot Worktree Diverged from Integration Branch\n27310 \" ✓ Suite Snapshot Synchronized with Integration Branch for WP-1103 AC2 Re-Run\n27311 10:19a ✓ Work State Updated: WP-1103 AC2 Full Suite Run 8783 Active\n27313 10:31a ○ Suite Process PID 1579239 Running from pr396-takeover Worktree, Not Suite Snapshot\n27314 \" ○ nonprogress_recovery.test.ts Does Not Exist in Suite Snapshot Worktree\n27315 \" ○ Suite Snapshot Runner Confirmed Active — pr396-takeover Running Parallel Test Suite from nexus-code Main\n27316 \" ○ pr396-takeover Suite Uses nexus-code Main Checkout node_modules Despite Running from pr396-takeover\n27317 \" ○ pr396-takeover Partial Suite Run Spawned by a Different Claude Session\n\nAccess 50k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only. Worker runtime: use Smart search by default: follow the mem-search skill in three steps—search({query, project}) for an index, timeline({anchor}) for context around relevant results, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records you choose after reviewing the index and context. Do not use auto or guided modes. Optional Dumb search, dumb_search({query, project}): Doesn’t reason about the results. Fast, but shallow. Use Smart for reliable recall. A hosted read-only connector may expose searches without write tools; do not call a missing write tool.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19b9f-f23a-70e0-bbf9-0adf509bb26d","create_time":1793615573.9680917,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
