{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:01:00.954Z","ordinal":41002,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19c21-eae7-7351-8f59-ab15f352b0bf","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-748d43e0-c029-45d1-bd41-2012a7e3d381","process_id":"63785","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","cat /home/mike/.codex/memories/skills/nexus-release-qualification/SKILL.md; sed -n '245,285p' cli/test/sidecar.test.ts; sed -n '130,205p' cli/test/tui_surface_e2e.test.ts; sed -n '210,280p' cli/test/upgrade_tui.test.ts; rg -n \"process-scope|test-scope-procs|SUITE\" scripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-suite-snapshot","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /home/mike/.codex/memories/skills/nexus-release-qualification/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":"/home/mike/.codex/memories/skills/nexus-release-qualification/SKILL.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '245,285p' cli/test/sidecar.test.ts","name":"sidecar.test.ts","path":"cli/test/sidecar.test.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '130,205p' cli/test/tui_surface_e2e.test.ts","name":"tui_surface_e2e.test.ts","path":"cli/test/tui_surface_e2e.test.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '210,280p' cli/test/upgrade_tui.test.ts","name":"upgrade_tui.test.ts","path":"cli/test/upgrade_tui.test.ts"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'process-scope|test-scope-procs|SUITE' scripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md","query":"process-scope|test-scope-procs|SUITE","path":"test-scope-procs.sh"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"---\nname: nexus-release-qualification\ndescription: Coordinate or verify a Nexus RC/release lane when claims, exact-head CI, artifact integrity, reproducibility, or installed-PTY qualification are in scope.\nargument-hint: \"[rc-version or release lane]\"\nuser-invocable: false\nallowed-tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash\n---\n\n# Nexus Release Qualification\n\n## When to use\n\n- The task concerns a Nexus v1 RC/release lane, recovery after an interrupted run, or an exact-artifact qualification claim.\n- The task needs to distinguish source/CI acceptance, artifact evidence, installed-RC qualification, and publication.\n- Do not use this to bypass another owner's claim, access held-out material, or publish/tag/push without explicit ownership.\n\n## Inputs / context to gather\n\n1. Read `/home/mike/nexus-code/AGENTS.md`, `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`, `docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md`, current work state, `.git/nexus-claims`, worktrees, and relevant PR/CI exact heads.\n2. Snapshot the shared checkout's branch, HEAD, porcelain state, and ownership before any mutation. Treat a dirty shared checkout as read-only.\n3. For `$ARGUMENTS`, identify the exact tag, source commit, archive digest, installed artifact path, claims, and gate(s) requested.\n\n## Procedure\n\n1. Establish ownership. Verify host identity, boot identity if recovery is involved, process start time, command, working directory, and claim age. Obtain explicit handoff before touching another lane.\n2. Work only in a claimed isolated worktree with isolated `HOME`/XDG state. Claim `SUITE` before a full matrix and `GATEWAY` before synthetic gateway work. Never use `pkill -f` or `killall`.\n3. Separate status: source test/CI, independent review, artifact integrity, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC scripted PTY, held-out/provider/standalone acceptance, and publication. Report each gate separately.\n4. For artifact integrity, verify tag object -> source commit -> archive digest; compare release metadata, `SHA256SUMS`, provenance/SBOM/manifests, installer/version/help, and evidence packet checksum index. Preserve byte-faithful API captures.\n5. For reproducibility, build the exact RC on distinct runners, compare runner outputs to each other and public assets byte-for-byte, then retain checksum evidence. Avoid overlapping full CI matrices.\n6. For installed PTY qualification, rerun every required scripted scenario against the freshly installed exact artifact using isolated HOME/workspace and process-cleanup evidence. Do not substitute historic notes or source-level tests.\n7. For cancellation remediation, confirm child liveness before cancel; assert `INTERRUPTED`, settled outstanding tool state, no post-cancel mutation, and shell/child exit. Compare only with an exact archived RC core.\n\n## Efficiency plan\n\n- Read claims/topology once and cache exact head/tag/digest plus gate status in the work-state update.\n- Run focused gate-specific checks before any serialized full suite. Cancel only an identified duplicate suite, never a different owner’s run.\n- Stop a readiness claim immediately when an exact-artifact or ownership invariant is missing; record the unresolved gate rather than broadening scope.\n\n## Pitfalls and fixes\n\n- Green CI or an accepted source review is not RC/product qualification -> require the exact installed artifact and documented acceptance gates.\n- Reboot, tmpfs recreation, or an inaccessible WSL path is not durable recovery evidence -> inspect durable state on the actual host/filesystem.\n- `release-assets.json` is an object -> enumerate `.assets`.\n- A dirty checkout can make `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` fail on cleanliness -> use a clean committed snapshot for that gate.\n- Sidecar tests do not prove TUI Escape behavior -> rerun the exact-artifact scripted PTY scenario.\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n- Shared checkout was preserved; worktree, claims, and isolated HOME/XDG are recorded.\n- Exact head/tag/artifact digest and CI state are recorded.\n- Every stated gate has a separate pass/fail/unverified disposition.\n- Artifact and reproducibility evidence includes retained checksums.\n- Installed-RC PTY evidence is fresh, exact-artifact, and includes process cleanup.\n- Held-out, owner-only, and publication boundaries were preserved.\n      assert.doesNotMatch(req.preview, /abcdef1234567890/);\n      await send({ type: \"deny\", id: req.id });\n      await server.idle();\n    });\n  });\n\n  test(\"an unknown approval id is reported, not ignored\", async () => {\n    await withSidecar(writeTurn, \"review\", async ({ events, send }) => {\n      await send({ type: \"approve\", id: \"approval-999\" });\n      const err = events.find((e) => e.type === \"error\");\n      assert.equal(err.code, \"NO_PENDING_APPROVAL\");\n      assert.equal(err.id, \"approval-999\");\n    });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"SidecarServer: cancellation\", () => {\n  test(\"cancel during inference ends the turn INTERRUPTED promptly\", async () => {\n    await withSidecar(() => ({ kind: \"text\", content: \"slow answer\", delayMs: 3000 }), \"auto\", async ({ server, events, send }) => {\n      const started = Date.now();\n      await send({ type: \"prompt.submit\", id: \"t1\", text: \"x\" });\n      await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 200));\n      await send({ type: \"cancel\" });\n      await server.idle();\n      assert.ok(Date.now() - started < 2500, \"turn ended well before the gateway replied\");\n      const result = events.find((e) => e.type === \"turn.result\");\n      assert.equal(result.turn.execution, \"INTERRUPTED\");\n      assert.equal(result.turn.outcome, \"NOT_ESTABLISHED\");\n    });\n  });\n\n  test(\"cancel sent immediately after submit is not lost\", async () => {\n    await withSidecar(() => ({ kind: \"text\", content: \"slow answer\", delayMs: 3000 }), \"auto\", async ({ server, events, send }) => {\n      await send({ type: \"prompt.submit\", id: \"t1\", text: \"x\" });\n      await send({ type: \"cancel\" });\n      await server.idle();\n      assert.equal(events.find((e) => e.type === \"turn.result\").turn.execution, \"INTERRUPTED\");\n    });\n  });\n\n  test(\"cancel while an approval is pending denies it and interrupts the turn\", async () => {\n      child.stdout.on(\"data\", (c) => (out += c));\n      child.stderr.on(\"data\", (c) => (err += c));\n      child.on(\"close\", (c) => resolve({ code: c, out, err }));\n    });\n    assert.equal(code, 0, `driver failed:\\n${err}\\n${out.slice(-3000)}`);\n    const r = JSON.parse(out.trim().split(\"\\n\").pop()!);\n    const events = lines(plan.env.NEXUS_RECORD_EVENTS);\n    const commands = lines(plan.env.NEXUS_RECORD_COMMANDS);\n    let head = \"unknown\";\n    try {\n      head = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"], { cwd: ROOT, encoding: \"utf8\" }).trim();\n    } catch {}\n    const metrics = path.join(EVIDENCE, \"tui_surface.metrics.json\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(metrics, JSON.stringify({ run: { id: randomUUID(), generatedAt: new Date().toISOString(), gitHead: head, tuiSha256: sha256(TUI), sidecarSha256: sha256(SIDECAR) }, ...r }, null, 2) + \"\\n\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(EVIDENCE, \"tui_surface.manifest.json\"), JSON.stringify({ files: Object.fromEntries([plan.cast, plan.screens, metrics].map((f) => [path.basename(f), sha256(f)])) }, null, 2) + \"\\n\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(EVIDENCE, \"events.ndjson\"), events.map((e) => JSON.stringify(e)).join(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(EVIDENCE, \"commands.ndjson\"), commands.map((e) => JSON.stringify(e)).join(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\");\n    assert.ok(r.recording.monotonic, \"recording timestamps never go backwards\");\n    const outcomes = events.filter((e) => e.type === \"turn.result\").map((e) => [e.turn.execution, e.turn.outcome, e.turn.reason ?? null]);\n    assert.ok(outcomes.length >= 8, JSON.stringify(outcomes));\n    assert.deepEqual(outcomes.map((o) => o[2]).slice(0, 7), [null, \"VERIFICATION_NOT_RUN\", \"VERIFICATION_NOT_RUN\", \"VERIFICATION_NOT_RUN\", \"OPERATOR_INTERRUPT\", \"REQUIREMENTS_INCOMPLETE\", \"VERIFIER_FAILED\"]);\n    if (process.env.NEXUS_SURFACE_AUDIT === \"1\") return; // audit runs only capture\n    // Assertions are added with the acceptance matrix (see docs/reviews/NEXUS_TUI_SURFACE_2026-10-12.md).\n    assertSurface(r, events, commands, shows);\n  } finally {\n    await gw.close();\n    fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    fs.rmSync(home, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\nfunction assertSurface(r: any, events: any[], commands: any[], shows: (screen: string[], text: string) => boolean): void {\n  const screens: Record<string, string[]> = r.screens;\n  const all = Object.values(screens).flat();\n  // Outcomes in words, never raw fields; each outcome kind appears.\n  assert.ok(!all.some((l) => l.includes(\"execution=\") || l.includes(\"TURN ENDED\") || l.includes(\"0 tool call\")), \"raw outcome fields stay in the receipt\");\n  for (const title of [\"✓ Done\", \"! Done · not verified\", \"◌ Cancelled\", \"× Verification failed\", \"! Requirements still open\"]) {\n    assert.ok(all.some((l) => l.includes(title)), `outcome ${title} shown`);\n  }\n  // Markdown rendered, no markers left.\n  const md = screens[\"03-markdown-final\"];\n  for (const marker of [\"**\", \"```\", \"## \", \"|---\"]) assert.ok(!md.some((l) => l.includes(marker)), `markdown marker ${marker} left`);\n  assert.ok(shows(md, \"Cache layer plan\") && md.some((l) => l.includes(\"Option │ Default\")) && md.some((l) => l.includes(\"↪\")), md.join(\"\\n\"));\n  // Streaming showed no raw markers either.\n  assert.ok(!screens[\"02-streaming\"].some((l) => l.includes(\"**\") || l.includes(\"## \")), screens[\"02-streaming\"].join(\"\\n\"));\n  // Tools: bounded command output with an exact count; a failed read stays failed.\n  const tools = screens[\"07-tools-final\"];\n  assert.ok(tools.some((l) => l.includes(\"exit 0 · 121 lines\")) && tools.some((l) => l.includes(\"… 115 earlier lines\")), tools.join(\"\\n\"));\n  assert.ok(tools.some((l) => l.includes(\"esc:\") && l.includes(\"end\")), `the output's last line is shown: ${tools.join(\"\\n\")}`);\n  assert.ok(tools.some((l) => l.includes(\"× Read missing.txt\")), tools.join(\"\\n\"));\n  assert.equal(r.raw_has_file_escape, false, \"the OSC 52 sequence printed by the command never reached the terminal\");\n  // One activity indicator: the status bar never animates.\n  const spinner = /[⠋⠙⠹⠸⠼⠴⠦⠧⠇⠏]/;\n  for (const [name, rows] of Object.entries(screens)) assert.ok(!spinner.test(rows[0]), `${name}: status bar shows no spinner`);\n  assert.ok(spinner.test(screens[\"04-slow-inference\"].at(-2)!) && shows(screens[\"04-slow-inference\"], \"thinking\"), screens[\"04-slow-inference\"].join(\"\\n\"));\n  // Scrolling: position kept, new output announced.\n  assert.ok(r.scroll_kept, \"the reading position is kept while output arrives\");\n  assert.ok(shows(screens[\"06-scrolled-back-new-output\"], \"↓ new output\"), screens[\"06-scrolled-back-new-output\"].join(\"\\n\"));\n  // Steering: one steer command, queued then applied.\n  assert.equal(commands.filter((c) => c.type === \"steer\").length, 1);\n  assert.deepEqual(events.filter((e) => e.type === \"steer.ack\").map((e) => e.status), [\"queued\", \"applied\"]);\n  // Paste: the sent text is visible under its label.\n  assert.ok(shows(screens[\"07-tools-final\"].concat(all), \"line one of the note\"), \"pasted text shown\");\n  // Approval: target and decisions with focus; buffered keys did not decide.\n  const approval = screens[\"10-approval\"];\n  assert.ok(shows(approval, \"Approval needed\") && shows(approval, \"Proposed: create config.json\") && shows(approval, \"Approve all later actions\") && !shows(approval, \"y Approve\"), approval.join(\"\\n\"));\n  assert.ok(r.approval_survived_buffered_keys);\n  assert.ok(r.letters_disarmed_hint, \"keys typed just before the panel disarm its letters, and the panel says so\");\n  // Requirements: listed once, and the repeated replies are explained.\n  const req = screens[\"14-requirements-incomplete\"];\n  assert.ok(shows(req, \"R1 [open] add a README section\") && shows(req, \"asked the agent to continue\"), req.join(\"\\n\"));\n  assert.ok(!req.some((l) => l.includes(\"handled.Both\")), \"replies are not run together\");\n  // Verification failure names the command.\n  assert.ok(shows(screens[\"13-verification-failed\"], \"npm test failed\"), screens[\"13-verification-failed\"].join(\"\\n\"));\n  // Narrow and short windows: nothing wider than the terminal; the composer line is kept.\n  for (const [name, width] of [[\"19-narrow\", 60], [\"21-resize-during-stream\", 64], [\"20-short\", 80]] as const) {\n      assert.equal(outcome.kind, \"reply\");\n      if (outcome.kind === \"reply\") {\n        assert.equal(outcome.success, true, outcome.output);\n        assert.match(outcome.output, /Nexus successfully upgraded to v1\\.0\\.0/);\n        assert.match(outcome.output, /Restart Nexus to activate the new version/);\n      }\n\n      // Verify symlink was swapped to v1.0.0\n      const activeLink = fs.readlinkSync(path.join(binDir, \"nexus\"));\n      assert.equal(activeLink, path.join(prefix, \"lib\", \"nexus\", \"v1.0.0\", \"bin\", \"nexus\"));\n    } finally {\n      process.env.NEXUS_HOME = prevHome;\n    }\n  });\n\n  it(\"leaves installation untouched when deliberate approval is declined in TUI\", async () => {\n    const prefix = path.join(tmpRoot, \"pkg-declined\");\n    const oldVersion = \"v0.1.0-alpha.2\";\n    const verDir = path.join(prefix, \"lib\", \"nexus\", oldVersion);\n    const binDir = path.join(prefix, \"bin\");\n    fs.mkdirSync(path.join(verDir, \"bin\"), { recursive: true });\n    fs.mkdirSync(binDir, { recursive: true });\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(verDir, \"VERSION\"), `${oldVersion}\\n`);\n\n    const oldBin = path.join(verDir, \"bin\", \"nexus\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(oldBin, `#!/bin/sh\\necho \"nexus ${oldVersion}\"\\n`);\n    fs.chmodSync(oldBin, 0o755);\n    fs.symlinkSync(oldBin, path.join(binDir, \"nexus\"));\n\n    const prevHome = process.env.NEXUS_HOME;\n    process.env.NEXUS_HOME = verDir;\n\n    const host: SlashHost = {\n      app: {} as any,\n      mode: () => \"auto\" as any,\n      setMode: () => {},\n      sessionId: () => \"test-session\",\n      setSessionId: () => {},\n      checkpoints: () => ({} as any),\n      setWorkspace: () => {},\n      saveSession: () => {},\n      resumeSession: () => ({ ok: true, message: \"\" }),\n      history: () => [],\n      confirm: () => undefined,\n      requestApproval: async () => false, // Operator declines!\n      receipt: () => [],\n    };\n\n    try {\n      const outcome = await routeSlash(host, \"upgrade\", \"\", new AbortController().signal);\n      assert.equal(outcome.kind, \"reply\");\n      if (outcome.kind === \"reply\") {\n        assert.equal(outcome.success, false);\n        assert.match(outcome.output, /Upgrade to v1\\.0\\.0 was declined/);\n      }\n\n      // Verify link remains old version\n      const activeLink = fs.readlinkSync(path.join(binDir, \"nexus\"));\n      assert.equal(activeLink, oldBin);\n      assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(prefix, \"lib\", \"nexus\", \"v1.0.0\")), false);\n    } finally {\n      process.env.NEXUS_HOME = prevHome;\n    }\n  });\n});\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:50:| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:132:  echo \"summary gate accepted an unavailable process-scope measurement\" >&2\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":175249308}},"started_at_ms":1793620859777,"completed_at_ms":1793620860953}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:01:02.759Z","ordinal":41003,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19c22-6726-73b3-8e04-94335646796e","call_id":"call_bd58c4b71ed34bfeb78c52d47e78e1fc","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 8.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---\nname: nexus-release-qualification\ndescription: Coordinate or verify a Nexus RC/release lane when claims, exact-head CI, artifact integrity, reproducibility, or installed-PTY qualification are in scope.\nargument-hint: \"[rc-version or release lane]\"\nuser-invocable: false\nallowed-tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash\n---\n\n# Nexus Release Qualification\n\n## When to use\n\n- The task concerns a Nexus v1 RC/release lane, recovery after an interrupted run, or an exact-artifact qualification claim.\n- The task needs to distinguish source/CI acceptance, artifact evidence, installed-RC qualification, and publication.\n- Do not use this to bypass another owner's claim, access held-out material, or publish/tag/push without explicit ownership.\n\n## Inputs / context to gather\n\n1. Read `/home/mike/nexus-code/AGENTS.md`, `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`, `docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md`, current work state, `.git/nexus-claims`, worktrees, and relevant PR/CI exact heads.\n2. Snapshot the shared checkout's branch, HEAD, porcelain state, and ownership before any mutation. Treat a dirty shared checkout as read-only.\n3. For `$ARGUMENTS`, identify the exact tag, source commit, archive digest, installed artifact path, claims, and gate(s) requested.\n\n## Procedure\n\n1. Establish ownership. Verify host identity, boot identity if recovery is involved, process start time, command, working directory, and claim age. Obtain explicit handoff before touching another lane.\n2. Work only in a claimed isolated worktree with isolated `HOME`/XDG state. Claim `SUITE` before a full matrix and `GATEWAY` before synthetic gateway work. Never use `pkill -f` or `killall`.\n3. Separate status: source test/CI, independent review, artifact integrity, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC scripted PTY, held-out/provider/standalone acceptance, and publication. Report each gate separately.\n4. For artifact integrity, verify tag object -> source commit -> archive digest; compare release metadata, `SHA256SUMS`, provenance/SBOM/manifests, installer/version/help, and evidence packet checksum index. Preserve byte-faithful API captures.\n5. For reproducibility, build the exact RC on distinct runners, compare runner outputs to each other and public assets byte-for-byte, then retain checksum evidence. Avoid overlapping full CI matrices.\n6. For installed PTY qualification, rerun every required scripted scenario against the freshly installed exact artifact using isolated HOME/workspace and process-cleanup evidence. Do not substitute historic notes or source-level tests.\n7. For cancellation remediation, confirm child liveness before cancel; assert `INTERRUPTED`, settled outstanding tool state, no post-cancel mutation, and shell/child exit. Compare only with an exact archived RC core.\n\n## Efficiency plan\n\n- Read claims/topology once and cache exact head/tag/digest plus gate status in the work-state update.\n- Run focused gate-specific checks before any serialized full suite. Cancel only an identified duplicate suite, never a different owner’s run.\n- Stop a readiness claim immediately when an exact-artifact or ownership invariant is missing; record the unresolved gate rather than broadening scope.\n\n## Pitfalls and fixes\n\n- Green CI or an accepted source review is not RC/product qualification -> require the exact installed artifact and documented acceptance gates.\n- Reboot, tmpfs recreation, or an inaccessible WSL path is not durable recovery evidence -> inspect durable state on the actual host/filesystem.\n- `release-assets.json` is an object -> enumerate `.assets`.\n- A dirty checkout can make `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` fail on cleanliness -> use a clean committed snapshot for that gate.\n- Sidecar tests do not prove TUI Escape behavior -> rerun the exact-artifact scripted PTY scenario.\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n- Shared checkout was preserved; worktree, claims, and isolated HOME/XDG are recorded.\n- Exact head/tag/artifact digest and CI state are recorded.\n- Every stated gate has a separate pass/fail/unverified disposition.\n- Artifact and reproducibility evidence includes retained checksums.\n- Installed-RC PTY evidence is fresh, exact-artifact, and includes process cleanup.\n- Held-out, owner-only, and publication boundaries were preserved.\n      assert.doesNotMatch(req.preview, /abcdef1234567890/);\n      await send({ type: \"deny\", id: req.id });\n      await server.idle();\n    });\n  });\n\n  test(\"an unknown approval id is reported, not ignored\", async () => {\n    await withSidecar(writeTurn, \"review\", async ({ events, send }) => {\n      await send({ type: \"approve\", id: \"approval-999\" });\n      const err = events.find((e) => e.type === \"error\");\n      assert.equal(err.code, \"NO_PENDING_APPROVAL\");\n      assert.equal(err.id, \"approval-999\");\n    });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"SidecarServer: cancellation\", () => {\n  test(\"cancel during inference ends the turn INTERRUPTED promptly\", async () => {\n    await withSidecar(() => ({ kind: \"text\", content: \"slow answer\", delayMs: 3000 }), \"auto\", async ({ server, events, send }) => {\n      const started = Date.now();\n      await send({ type: \"prompt.submit\", id: \"t1\", text: \"x\" });\n      await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 200));\n      await send({ type: \"cancel\" });\n      await server.idle();\n      assert.ok(Date.now() - started < 2500, \"turn ended well before the gateway replied\");\n      const result = events.find((e) => e.type === \"turn.result\");\n      assert.equal(result.turn.execution, \"INTERRUPTED\");\n      assert.equal(result.turn.outcome, \"NOT_ESTABLISHED\");\n    });\n  });\n\n  test(\"cancel sent immediately after submit is not lost\", async () => {\n    await withSidecar(() => ({ kind: \"text\", content: \"slow answer\", delayMs: 3000 }), \"auto\", async ({ server, events, send }) => {\n      await send({ type: \"prompt.submit\", id: \"t1\", text: \"x\" });\n      await send({ type: \"cancel\" });\n      await server.idle();\n      assert.equal(events.find((e) => e.type === \"turn.result\").turn.execution, \"INTERRUPTED\");\n    });\n  });\n\n  test(\"cancel while an approval is pending denies it and interrupts the turn\", async () => {\n      child.stdout.on(\"data\", (c) => (out += c));\n      child.stderr.on(\"data\", (c) => (err += c));\n      child.on(\"close\", (c) => resolve({ code: c, out, err }));\n    });\n    assert.equal(code, 0, `driver failed:\\n${err}\\n${out.slice(-3000)}`);\n    const r = JSON.parse(out.trim().split(\"\\n\").pop()!);\n    const events = lines(plan.env.NEXUS_RECORD_EVENTS);\n    const commands = lines(plan.env.NEXUS_RECORD_COMMANDS);\n    let head = \"unknown\";\n    try {\n      head = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"], { cwd: ROOT, encoding: \"utf8\" }).trim();\n    } catch {}\n    const metrics = path.join(EVIDENCE, \"tui_surface.metrics.json\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(metrics, JSON.stringify({ run: { id: randomUUID(), generatedAt: new Date().toISOString(), gitHead: head, tuiSha256: sha256(TUI), sidecarSha256: sha256(SIDECAR) }, ...r }, null, 2) + \"\\n\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(EVIDENCE, \"tui_surface.manifest.json\"), JSON.stringify({ files: Object.fromEntries([plan.cast, plan.screens, metrics].map((f) => [path.basename(f), sha256(f)])) }, null, 2) + \"\\n\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(EVIDENCE, \"events.ndjson\"), events.map((e) => JSON.stringify(e)).join(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(EVIDENCE, \"commands.ndjson\"), commands.map((e) => JSON.stringify(e)).join(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\");\n    assert.ok(r.recording.monotonic, \"recording timestamps never go backwards\");\n    const outcomes = events.filter((e) => e.type === \"turn.result\").map((e) => [e.turn.execution, e.turn.outcome, e.turn.reason ?? null]);\n    assert.ok(outcomes.length >= 8, JSON.stringify(outcomes));\n    assert.deepEqual(outcomes.map((o) => o[2]).slice(0, 7), [null, \"VERIFICATION_NOT_RUN\", \"VERIFICATION_NOT_RUN\", \"VERIFICATION_NOT_RUN\", \"OPERATOR_INTERRUPT\", \"REQUIREMENTS_INCOMPLETE\", \"VERIFIER_FAILED\"]);\n    if (process.env.NEXUS_SURFACE_AUDIT === \"1\") return; // audit runs only capture\n    // Assertions are added with the acceptance matrix (see docs/reviews/NEXUS_TUI_SURFACE_2026-10-12.md).\n    assertSurface(r, events, commands, shows);\n  } finally {\n    await gw.close();\n    fs.rmSync(repo, { recursive: true, force: true });\n    fs.rmSync(home, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\nfunction assertSurface(r: any, events: any[], commands: any[], shows: (screen: string[], text: string) => boolean): void {\n  const screens: Record<string, string[]> = r.screens;\n  const all = Object.values(screens).flat();\n  // Outcomes in words, never raw fields; each outcome kind appears.\n  assert.ok(!all.some((l) => l.includes(\"execution=\") || l.includes(\"TURN ENDED\") || l.includes(\"0 tool call\")), \"raw outcome fields stay in the receipt\");\n  for (const title of [\"✓ Done\", \"! Done · not verified\", \"◌ Cancelled\", \"× Verification failed\", \"! Requirements still open\"]) {\n    assert.ok(all.some((l) => l.includes(title)), `outcome ${title} shown`);\n  }\n  // Markdown rendered, no markers left.\n  const md = screens[\"03-markdown-final\"];\n  for (const marker of [\"**\", \"```\", \"## \", \"|---\"]) assert.ok(!md.some((l) => l.includes(marker)), `markdown marker ${marker} left`);\n  assert.ok(shows(md, \"Cache layer plan\") && md.some((l) => l.includes(\"Option │ Default\")) && md.some((l) => l.includes(\"↪\")), md.join(\"\\n\"));\n  // Streaming showed no raw markers either.\n  assert.ok(!screens[\"02-streaming\"].some((l) => l.includes(\"**\") || l.includes(\"## \")), screens[\"02-streaming\"].join(\"\\n\"));\n  // Tools: bounded command output with an exact count; a failed read stays failed.\n  const tools = screens[\"07-tools-final\"];\n  assert.ok(tools.some((l) => l.includes(\"exit 0 · 121 lines\")) && tools.some((l) => l.includes(\"… 115 earlier lines\")), tools.join(\"\\n\"));\n  assert.ok(tools.some((l) => l.includes(\"esc:\") && l.includes(\"end\")), `the output's last line is shown: ${tools.join(\"\\n\")}`);\n  assert.ok(tools.some((l) => l.includes(\"× Read missing.txt\")), tools.join(\"\\n\"));\n  assert.equal(r.raw_has_file_escape, false, \"the OSC 52 sequence printed by the command never reached the terminal\");\n  // One activity indicator: the status bar never animates.\n  const spinner = /[⠋⠙⠹⠸⠼⠴⠦⠧⠇⠏]/;\n  for (const [name, rows] of Object.entries(screens)) assert.ok(!spinner.test(rows[0]), `${name}: status bar shows no spinner`);\n  assert.ok(spinner.test(screens[\"04-slow-inference\"].at(-2)!) && shows(screens[\"04-slow-inference\"], \"thinking\"), screens[\"04-slow-inference\"].join(\"\\n\"));\n  // Scrolling: position kept, new output announced.\n  assert.ok(r.scroll_kept, \"the reading position is kept while output arrives\");\n  assert.ok(shows(screens[\"06-scrolled-back-new-output\"], \"↓ new output\"), screens[\"06-scrolled-back-new-output\"].join(\"\\n\"));\n  // Steering: one steer command, queued then applied.\n  assert.equal(commands.filter((c) => c.type === \"steer\").length, 1);\n  assert.deepEqual(events.filter((e) => e.type === \"steer.ack\").map((e) => e.status), [\"queued\", \"applied\"]);\n  // Paste: the sent text is visible under its label.\n  assert.ok(shows(screens[\"07-tools-final\"].concat(all), \"line one of the note\"), \"pasted text shown\");\n  // Approval: target and decisions with focus; buffered keys did not decide.\n  const approval = screens[\"10-approval\"];\n  assert.ok(shows(approval, \"Approval needed\") && shows(approval, \"Proposed: create config.json\") && shows(approval, \"Approve all later actions\") && !shows(approval, \"y Approve\"), approval.join(\"\\n\"));\n  assert.ok(r.approval_survived_buffered_keys);\n  assert.ok(r.letters_disarmed_hint, \"keys typed just before the panel disarm its letters, and the panel says so\");\n  // Requirements: listed once, and the repeated replies are explained.\n  const req = screens[\"14-requirements-incomplete\"];\n  assert.ok(shows(req, \"R1 [open] add a README section\") && shows(req, \"asked the agent to continue\"), req.join(\"\\n\"));\n  assert.ok(!req.some((l) => l.includes(\"handled.Both\")), \"replies are not run together\");\n  // Verification failure names the command.\n  assert.ok(shows(screens[\"13-verification-failed\"], \"npm test failed\"), screens[\"13-verification-failed\"].join(\"\\n\"));\n  // Narrow and short windows: nothing wider than the terminal; the composer line is kept.\n  for (const [name, width] of [[\"19-narrow\", 60], [\"21-resize-during-stream\", 64], [\"20-short\", 80]] as const) {\n      assert.equal(outcome.kind, \"reply\");\n      if (outcome.kind === \"reply\") {\n        assert.equal(outcome.success, true, outcome.output);\n        assert.match(outcome.output, /Nexus successfully upgraded to v1\\.0\\.0/);\n        assert.match(outcome.output, /Restart Nexus to activate the new version/);\n      }\n\n      // Verify symlink was swapped to v1.0.0\n      const activeLink = fs.readlinkSync(path.join(binDir, \"nexus\"));\n      assert.equal(activeLink, path.join(prefix, \"lib\", \"nexus\", \"v1.0.0\", \"bin\", \"nexus\"));\n    } finally {\n      process.env.NEXUS_HOME = prevHome;\n    }\n  });\n\n  it(\"leaves installation untouched when deliberate approval is declined in TUI\", async () => {\n    const prefix = path.join(tmpRoot, \"pkg-declined\");\n    const oldVersion = \"v0.1.0-alpha.2\";\n    const verDir = path.join(prefix, \"lib\", \"nexus\", oldVersion);\n    const binDir = path.join(prefix, \"bin\");\n    fs.mkdirSync(path.join(verDir, \"bin\"), { recursive: true });\n    fs.mkdirSync(binDir, { recursive: true });\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(verDir, \"VERSION\"), `${oldVersion}\\n`);\n\n    const oldBin = path.join(verDir, \"bin\", \"nexus\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(oldBin, `#!/bin/sh\\necho \"nexus ${oldVersion}\"\\n`);\n    fs.chmodSync(oldBin, 0o755);\n    fs.symlinkSync(oldBin, path.join(binDir, \"nexus\"));\n\n    const prevHome = process.env.NEXUS_HOME;\n    process.env.NEXUS_HOME = verDir;\n\n    const host: SlashHost = {\n      app: {} as any,\n      mode: () => \"auto\" as any,\n      setMode: () => {},\n      sessionId: () => \"test-session\",\n      setSessionId: () => {},\n      checkpoints: () => ({} as any),\n      setWorkspace: () => {},\n      saveSession: () => {},\n      resumeSession: () => ({ ok: true, message: \"\" }),\n      history: () => [],\n      confirm: () => undefined,\n      requestApproval: async () => false, // Operator declines!\n      receipt: () => [],\n    };\n\n    try {\n      const outcome = await routeSlash(host, \"upgrade\", \"\", new AbortController().signal);\n      assert.equal(outcome.kind, \"reply\");\n      if (outcome.kind === \"reply\") {\n        assert.equal(outcome.success, false);\n        assert.match(outcome.output, /Upgrade to v1\\.0\\.0 was declined/);\n      }\n\n      // Verify link remains old version\n      const activeLink = fs.readlinkSync(path.join(binDir, \"nexus\"));\n      assert.equal(activeLink, oldBin);\n      assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(prefix, \"lib\", \"nexus\", \"v1.0.0\")), false);\n    } finally {\n      process.env.NEXUS_HOME = prevHome;\n    }\n  });\n});\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:50:| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:132:  echo \"summary gate accepted an unavailable process-scope measurement\" >&2\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19c21-eae7-7351-8f59-ab15f352b0bf","create_time":1793620862.7588875}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
