{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:08:12.076Z","ordinal":41341,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a19c28-f42c-7083-88fd-648f66ca8b40","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Deliverables: write a deck, report, page or other file the person asked for as a file and attach it as work_product before you finish. When you stop, claude-mem copies each attached file (and any deck, document, page, image or spreadsheet you wrote outside the source tree) into this project's deliverables bucket, ~/.claude-mem/deliverables/<project>/, and links it on the request's card in My Work.\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- v1.1.2-release: state=WP-1104 standalone eval slice closed (05c49df2, 2a94f62e). WP-1103 AC2 mount-view test implemented and passing in live full suite. Reconciled claim metadata. Full test suite active., phase=GREEN, gate=AC2 focused PASS 3/3; full npm test live at 101m; upgrade rollback transaction group and D3 timeout lifecycle passed; final aggregate and scope postcheck pending, next=Keep suite session 8783 active through end; capture totals and postcheck, verify candidate evidence hash and send final independent review for WP-1103., friction=Intermittent filesystem journal waits delay upgrade transaction tests; all completed cases have passed, runner still active., updated=2026-11-02T12:00:00Z, reviewer=/root/review_delta, verdict=APPROVED for 05c49df2 and 2a94f62e, retrieval=nexus-test eval_integrity.test.ts:1729 SSE tool-call stream; eval_harness.test.ts:43 deterministic reply pattern; provider_connect.test.ts:31 local provider harness, updated 8 minutes ago\n- ...783 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-11-02 12:08pm UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 25 obs (10,130t read) | 47,805t work | 79% savings\n\n### Nov 2, 2026\n27408 11:41a ○ upgrade.test.ts Upgrade Journal, Crash Recovery & PATH Shadowing Group Passed\n27412 11:43a ○ Fifth jbd2 Stall — New Grandchild PID 2084643 Blocked at 2:12 Elapsed\n27413 \" ○ Fifth jbd2 Stall Is on upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts\n27414 11:45a ○ Fifth jbd2 Stall Resolved — upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts Continuing After ~4 Minutes\n27415 11:51a ○ System-Wide I/O Pressure ~22% During upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts jbd2 Stall\n27416 11:55a ○ upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts Second jbd2 Stall Resolved at ~13 Minutes\n27417 11:56a ○ upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts Completed — \"live transaction exceptions\" Group Took 739 Seconds Total\n27418 11:57a ✓ Work State Updated: WP-1103 Suite at 98 Minutes, upgrade_transaction_recovery Destructive Boundary Tests All Passed\n27419 11:58a ○ Sixth jbd2 Stall — New Grandchild PID 2167569 Blocked at 1:48 Elapsed\n27420 \" ○ Sixth jbd2 Stall Is on upgrade_tui.test.ts\n27421 \" ○ upgrade_tui.test.ts jbd2 Stall Resolved — Suite Log Advanced 81 Lines, TUI Tests Active\n27422 11:59a ○ Suite Log at 10,070 Lines — Verifier and Runner Tests Active, No Active Stall\n27423 12:00p ○ D3 Timeout Lifecycle Test Validates HTTP 500 / UNKNOWN Status Recovery Exhaustion\n27424 \" ○ Suite Run 8783 Completed: 2133 Pass, 3 Fail, 2 Skipped — Three Test Failures Identified\n27425 \" ○ Suite Snapshot Worktree Has 7 Modified Files and 7 Untracked Files Including WP-1103/1104 Additions\n27426 12:01p ○ Three Suite Failures Cross-Referenced Against SKILL.md Expected Behavior — Two Likely Timing Flakes, One Mock Server Issue\n27427 \" ○ Suite Runner Process Tree Gone — Suite Run 8783 Fully Exited, SUITE Claim Still Held\n27428 \" ✓ SUITE Claim Released — Suite Run 8783 Logged as FAIL with 2133/3/2 Result and Log SHA256\n27429 \" ○ upgrade_tui.test.ts Has Its Own Mock Server Setup — Server Start/Stop Scoped to the describe Block\n27430 \" ○ Audit Agents Completed: No Safe Next Slice; roadmap_status_audit Reported Different Suite Results Than Run 8783\n27431 12:02p ○ sidecar.test.ts Cancel Timing Test Fails Reproducibly in Isolation — Not a Flake from Suite Load\n27432 \" ○ sidecar.test.ts Cancel Test: Timing Assertion Checks \"Well Before Gateway Replied\" — Gateway Delay Is Only 2000ms in Test, Not 3000ms\n27433 \" ○ sidecar Cancel Test Root Cause: delayMs=3000 Gateway + 200ms Wait = Turn Can't Complete in <2500ms\n27434 \" ○ SidecarServer.cancel() Aborts turnAbort Signal But idle() Still Awaits activeTurn — Cancel May Not Interrupt HTTP Fetch\n27437 \" ○ upgrade_tui.test.ts Mock Server Failure Root Cause: NEXUS_RELEASES_API Set in before() but Failed to Reach the Test\n\nAccess 48k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only. Worker runtime: use Smart search by default: follow the mem-search skill in three steps—search({query, project}) for an index, timeline({anchor}) for context around relevant results, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records you choose after reviewing the index and context. Do not use auto or guided modes. Optional Dumb search, dumb_search({query, project}): Doesn’t reason about the results. Fast, but shallow. Use Smart for reliable recall. A hosted read-only connector may expose searches without write tools; do not call a missing write tool.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19c21-eae7-7351-8f59-ab15f352b0bf","create_time":1793621292.076723,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
