{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:22:27.985Z","ordinal":42141,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016ae88082cfe481a3b6aeeef4ad5424d6","status":"completed","call_id":"call_59d51160af1f4d0c9857496c9f549c43","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,180p' docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-scope-reconciliation tag -l 'v1.1.2*'; git ls-remote --tags origin 'refs/tags/v1.1.2*'\",\"workdir\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-scope-reconciliation\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":1200}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19c35-8dbf-7b72-9a43-c0e91b05ed32","create_time":1793622146.8135347}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:22:28.036Z","ordinal":42142,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19c35-8dbf-7b72-9a43-c0e91b05ed32","session_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","root_turn_id":"01a19c35-8dbf-7b72-9a43-c0e91b05ed32","response_id":"resp_0fd4138577b17921016ae88080fd6081a398150c7c1475ee07","usage":{"input_tokens":144489,"cached_input_tokens":143232,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":313,"reasoning_output_tokens":183,"total_tokens":144802},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":571216,"cached_input_tokens":565120,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2270,"reasoning_output_tokens":1606,"total_tokens":573486},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":809126152,"cached_input_tokens":802198400,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1696990,"reasoning_output_tokens":866191,"total_tokens":810823142}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:22:30.521Z","ordinal":42143,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19c35-8dbf-7b72-9a43-c0e91b05ed32","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-35372c47-98af-4928-81a7-7da758749308","process_id":"29879","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,180p' docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-scope-reconciliation tag -l 'v1.1.2*'; git ls-remote --tags origin 'refs/tags/v1.1.2*'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-scope-reconciliation","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '1,180p' docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-scope-reconciliation tag -l 'v1.1.2*'; git ls-remote --tags origin 'refs/tags/v1.1.2*'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Nexus Code v1.1.2-rc.1\n\n**Release Candidate 1 for Nexus Code v1.1.2**: a patch release on the v1.1.1 line with one operation message-delivery fix.\n\n## Fixed\n\n### A crash-resumed unit no longer receives a multi-message prompt's later messages twice\n\nWhen a work unit's prompt carried two or more operator or inter-unit messages, and Nexus stopped after submitting that prompt but before the unit's result was saved, resume recognised only the **first** message as already submitted. Every later message from that prompt was injected into the unit's conversation again.\n\nResume now recognises each message in a submitted prompt's messages block, whatever its position. Matching is still limited to prompts that Nexus issued (`isSubmittedUnitPrompt`, from v1.1.1), so marker text in model output, tool output, or files cannot suppress a message.\n\n- Impact in v1.1.1: the duplicated message was advisory context only. No message was lost, and no `TurnResult`, verification, or acceptance outcome was affected.\n- Regression coverage: the post-prompt crash test in `cli/test/operation_release_review.test.ts` now carries two messages. It asserts that each message appears once in the durable history and is acknowledged once.\n\n## Correction to the v1.1.1 notes\n\nThe v1.1.1 notes say that a recipient receives undelivered messages \"at most once\". That holds for prompts carrying a single message. For prompts carrying several messages, v1.1.1 could re-inject the second and later messages after a post-submission crash, as described above. v1.1.2 makes the statement hold in both cases. `docs/releases/v1.1.1.md` carries a matching addendum.\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\nUnchanged from v1.1.1: Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer, Node.js 22 or newer, and an OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint (local or an explicitly selected provider). The archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime.\n\n## Upgrade\n\nOperation records are unchanged: operation schema version 2, as in v1.1.1. No migration runs, and v1.1.1 can read records written by v1.1.2.\n\n## Qualification\n\nThis candidate inherits the v1.1.1 qualification record. The source change is limited to `cli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts` (`unsubmittedMessages` and a new `promptCarriesMessage` helper) and its test. Release qualification for this RC is the release workflow's gates (version, notes, provenance), plus independent review of the fix (PR #377) and of this candidate.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":2817799}},"started_at_ms":1793622149517,"completed_at_ms":1793622150521}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:22:31.854Z","ordinal":42144,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19c36-12ad-7230-8cc9-247b620f99e9","call_id":"call_59d51160af1f4d0c9857496c9f549c43","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"# Nexus Code v1.1.2-rc.1\n\n**Release Candidate 1 for Nexus Code v1.1.2**: a patch release on the v1.1.1 line with one operation message-delivery fix.\n\n## Fixed\n\n### A crash-resumed unit no longer receives a multi-message prompt's later messages twice\n\nWhen a work unit's prompt carried two or more operator or inter-unit messages, and Nexus stopped after submitting that prompt but before the unit's result was saved, resume recognised only the **first** message as already submitted. Every later message from that prompt was injected into the unit's conversation again.\n\nResume now recognises each message in a submitted prompt's messages block, whatever its position. Matching is still limited to prompts that Nexus issued (`isSubmittedUnitPrompt`, from v1.1.1), so marker text in model output, tool output, or files cannot suppress a message.\n\n- Impact in v1.1.1: the duplicated message was advisory context only. No message was lost, and no `TurnResult`, verification, or acceptance outcome was affected.\n- Regression coverage: the post-prompt crash test in `cli/test/operation_release_review.test.ts` now carries two messages. It asserts that each message appears once in the durable history and is acknowledged once.\n\n## Correction to the v1.1.1 notes\n\nThe v1.1.1 notes say that a recipient receives undelivered messages \"at most once\". That holds for prompts carrying a single message. For prompts carrying several messages, v1.1.1 could re-inject the second and later messages after a post-submission crash, as described above. v1.1.2 makes the statement hold in both cases. `docs/releases/v1.1.1.md` carries a matching addendum.\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\nUnchanged from v1.1.1: Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer, Node.js 22 or newer, and an OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint (local or an explicitly selected provider). The archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime.\n\n## Upgrade\n\nOperation records are unchanged: operation schema version 2, as in v1.1.1. No migration runs, and v1.1.1 can read records written by v1.1.2.\n\n## Qualification\n\nThis candidate inherits the v1.1.1 qualification record. The source change is limited to `cli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts` (`unsubmittedMessages` and a new `promptCarriesMessage` helper) and its test. Release qualification for this RC is the release workflow's gates (version, notes, provenance), plus independent review of the fix (PR #377) and of this candidate.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19c35-8dbf-7b72-9a43-c0e91b05ed32","create_time":1793622151.853882}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
