{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:26:41.703Z","ordinal":42365,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19c35-8dbf-7b72-9a43-c0e91b05ed32","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-71d32055-3b6f-4f8c-a6db-e445f17b6b17","process_id":"24147","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","nl -ba docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md | sed -n '65,125p'; nl -ba docs/v1.1.0/WP-1108-TRIAGE.md | sed -n '160,230p'; nl -ba docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md | sed -n '40,61p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-scope-reconciliation","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md","name":"WP-1104-PLAN.md","path":"docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba docs/v1.1.0/WP-1108-TRIAGE.md","name":"WP-1108-TRIAGE.md","path":"docs/v1.1.0/WP-1108-TRIAGE.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md","name":"ROADMAP.md","path":"docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"    65\t- **RED:** Strengthened `packaged evaluator runtime executes outside checkout` to invoke the packaged CLI and actual runner/scorer against a valid empty dataset; it failed because `eval/run.mjs` did not create `results.jsonl` when the selected split had no tasks.\n    66\t- **GREEN:** Pinned Bookworm package build completed; after extraction outside the checkout, `node --test eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` passed 3/3 with the actual installed `nexus eval` CLI, runner, and scorer. The rebuilt development artifact is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.1.tar.gz`; it is not exact-commit release evidence.\n    67\t- **Peer review:** Independent code review returned `APPROVED_WITH_COMMENTS` for AC2. Reviewer confirmed the installed CLI/runner/scorer path and the empty-split file fix; the comment is blocking AC4 evidence, which remains outstanding.\n    68\t- **AC3 test review:** A second independent read-only review confirmed that passing an invalid `NEXUS_HOME` and asserting the explicit `--limit` diagnostic wins establishes validation-before-runtime-resolution; assertions cover the score parent, score file and artifact directory remaining absent. The focused test has not yet been run because another worktree's test process is still live.\n    69\t- **AC5 test review:** An independent read-only review confirmed the non-empty two-task fixture and `--limit 1` assertions exercise real truncation and first-task-only prompting. The reviewer caught that `spawnSync` would block the in-process mock server; the test now uses async `spawn`, which the reviewer confirmed resolves that deadlock. Runtime verification remains pending the shared test lane.\n    70\t- **AC5 red/green:** The first strengthened run failed because the mock returned JSON while the client requested SSE (`INFERENCE_FAILED: stream_incomplete`). After switching to the retrieved SSE contract and setting `--workspace` to an isolated empty directory (so evaluator discovery cannot run this repository's test suite), `node cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs test/eval_cli.test.ts` passed 7/7; the non-empty `--limit 1` case confirmed exactly one completion request containing the first prompt and not the second.\n    71\t- **Six-task installed-candidate acceptance (2026-11-02):** The new `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance` acceptance test first failed with the expected missing-evidence assertion. A diagnostic run also confirmed that extracting an installed runtime below `/tmp` is rejected by the existing runtime root policy, so the test now extracts the archive into a fresh safe worktree path outside `/tmp` and the source checkout. A pinned Bookworm package was built from this integration worktree and its exact installed `bin/nexus` ran the `core-v1` benchmark split through a loopback deterministic fake provider. Focused test passed: 6/6 task invocations, 6 captured requests, no skipped or missing tasks, recomputed manifest SHA `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`; archive SHA `b385cd533f9e14bb161dba9a352d310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a`. Per-task hidden/regression validator and scorer outputs are retained in candidate-specific `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-b385cd533f9e.json`. The earlier generic `acceptance.json` is retained unchanged as superseded evidence; the test writes candidate evidence exclusively and rejects relative `hidden/...` command paths as well as full hidden validator commands in captured requests. This acceptance establishes execution coverage and request capture only; the deterministic `task_completed` fixture does not establish model quality, and its expected hidden checks are recorded as false.\n    72\t- **Independent review:** Initial re-review returned `REQUEST_CHANGES` to close WP-1103/1104 because six-task installed-candidate evidence was absent. Review of the first evidence found the relative hidden-command assertion too weak and the evidence write non-exclusive; both findings were addressed and the focused acceptance test passed again with candidate-specific evidence. Fresh full-slice re-review is pending.\n    73\t\n    74\t## Gate attempt notes\n    75\t\n    76\t- **Global release-scope guard:** Current `docs/releases/v1.1.2.md` still defines v1.1.2 as a patch on v1.1.1 containing one operation-message fix and inheriting v1.1.1 qualification. `docs/v1.1.0/README.md` also says WP-11xx is not implemented in its described release. This conflicts with the user's direction to complete the full WP-1101..WP-1108 roadmap in v1.1.2. The release definition, integrated branch, qualification and candidate must be reconciled to the full roadmap before any v1.1.2 publication; this WP slice does not change the release notes or release branch.\n    77\t- **Cross-slice audit (2026-11-02, independent read-only agents):** WP-1101 (`8a83c9e7`) has an unintegrated recorder prototype without runtime event wiring or branch-head gate evidence; WP-1102 (`ee7c8b1e`) has partial redaction work with operator acceptance pending; WP-1103 dataset/runner branches (`e430dab5`, `c548e53e`) have no PR, and required actual provider-request isolation, filesystem/mount denial, post-exit oracle scoring, and six-task G1.1-2 evidence are absent. WP-1105 has no implementation delta, WP-1106 has no branch or implementation, WP-1107 (`9cb5f6de`) is an unintegrated grammar generator prototype without provider-path integration, and WP-1108 (`550112cd`) is a partial modernization policy batch without branch-head gate evidence. None is release-qualified. These are audit leads; revalidate on the integrated exact head before marking any tracker item done.\n    78\t\n    79\t## Gate update — 2026-11-02\n    80\t\n    81\tThe notes above describe intermediate attempts and are superseded where they conflict with this gate update. After correcting the relative hidden-command checks and making evidence creation exclusive and candidate-specific, independent review by `/root/review_delta` returned **APPROVED** for the WP-1103/1104 source and six-task evidence. The reviewer did not rerun tests.\n    82\t\n    83\tThe final synchronized full-suite run completed with **2,138 tests, 2,136 passed, 0 failed, and 2 skipped**. The terminal process-scope postcheck reported `scope measurement fixtures passed`. Log: `/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-suite-snapshot/wp1104-suite-final-ac4.log`; SHA-256: `19aeb576f3be4f45b7507d79a0a1cfda1a46e9caebca59f87de9e60b17bf5a16`. The modified source and test files were byte-for-byte matched against the suite snapshot. `npm run build` passed on the integration worktree. The full-suite and process-scope claim was released after all test processes exited.\n    84\t\n    85\tInstalled-candidate evidence is recorded in `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-b385cd533f9e-suite.json` for package archive SHA-256 `b385cd533f9e14bb161dba9a352d310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a`. It records all six benchmark tasks and captured requests, with no missing or skipped task. The loopback deterministic provider does not establish model quality: its task-completion responses are not solutions, and hidden checks are recorded false. This is dataset execution and request-isolation evidence only. Per the 2026-11-02 coordinator ruling, this mock-only acceptance does not consume the GATEWAY claim; any remote/provider-backed inference still requires that claim.\n    86\t\n    87\tThis gate closes the WP-1103/1104 source slice only. It does not qualify a tagged release artifact or satisfy the full WP-1101..WP-1108 roadmap. `docs/releases/v1.1.2.md` still describes a narrower patch and must be reconciled with the user's full-roadmap scope before publication. The built archive predates the source commit and does not carry an explicit source-commit binding; it is not exact-commit release evidence.\n    88\t\n    89\t### WP-1104 tracker closeout\n    90\t\n    91\t- **Status:** done for the standalone CLI, package runtime closure, and six-task dataset execution acceptance delivered by this slice.\n    92\t- **Commit:** `05c49df2` (`feat(eval): package and run the versioned evaluator`).\n    93\t- **Test evidence:** `npm test` completed with 2,138 tests, 2,136 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped; process-scope postcheck passed. Log SHA-256: `19aeb576f3be4f45b7507d79a0a1cfda1a46e9caebca59f87de9e60b17bf5a16`.\n    94\t- **Type/build gate:** `npm run build` passed on the committed source tree.\n    95\t- **Independent review:** `/root/review_delta` returned **APPROVED** for commit `05c49df2`, including the gate record and candidate evidence; reviewer did not rerun the suite.\n    96\t- **Retrieval log:** XERJ entries above, including `nexus-test/eval_integrity.test.ts:1729` and `nexus-test/eval_harness.test.ts:43`.\n    97\t- **Release qualification boundary:** this tracker closeout is not exact-tag or publication approval; retain the full-roadmap and release-scope guards above.\n    98\t\n    99\t- A first `npm test` run on `/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-suite-snapshot` was diagnostic only: the snapshot had no `cli/dist/index.js` or Rust core binaries, and `NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT` was unset so the actual package smoke was skipped. Its test runner reported 1,981 tests (1,739 pass, 222 fail) and then remained in `turn_semantics.test.ts` with repeated provider-recovery retries; that process was interrupted after about 40 minutes. This is not accepted full-suite evidence.\n   100\t- Snapshot prerequisites are now built: `npm run build` and debug `cargo build --locked --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui` passed. Release core binaries were copied from the successful pinned Bookworm package build, whose Rust sources are unchanged by this WP-1104 slice.\n   101\t- A separate focused test process in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/pr398-review` remains active. The next full-suite attempt must wait for it to finish, then set `NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT` to the freshly extracted development package so the actual outside-checkout runtime test runs instead of skipping.\n   102\t- After peer review identified that the former empty-dataset `--limit 0` case did not prove truncation, the legacy compatibility test was strengthened to a non-empty two-task fixture and async local OpenAI-compatible mock. The first mock response format caused an expected transport failure; the second run timed out because the evaluator used the repository as its workspace and discovered the repository test command. Both causes were corrected. Current targeted TypeScript no-emit and `git diff --check` pass, and the updated focused suite passes 7/7.\n   103\t- AC4 can use the deterministic local fake provider and payload capture specified in `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md`; no public provider is needed for the dataset-isolation acceptance. The release concurrency plan still requires the serial `GATEWAY` claim for evaluator runs. That claim is held by `codex-root` on `ubuntu-desktop` for RC15 E5 provider verification (since 2026-10-31T09:47Z, no PID). This host is `mike-dev`, has a different boot ID, and has no matching process; the claimed worktree remains with untracked RC15 evidence. A handoff/stale determination is not supportable locally, so a conflict/handoff request was appended to the shared claim log and the claim/worktree remain untouched.\nnl: docs/v1.1.0/WP-1108-TRIAGE.md: No such file or directory\n    40\t### Work Packages\n    41\t\n    42\t| ID | Title | Summary & Deliverables | Backlog / Audit Source |\n    43\t| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n    44\t| **WP-1101** | **OpenTelemetry Local Tracing** | Implement `cli/src/core/trace.ts` providing hierarchical tracing conforming to OpenTelemetry GenAI semantics. Captures agent turn roots, model request spans, tool execution spans, and context compactions into local `trace.jsonl` files. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.1 |\n    45\t| **WP-1102** | **Flight Recorder Credential Redaction** | Implement automated zero-leak credential sanitization across all recorded spans, CLI error dumps, and debug journals, validating against the test fixtures in `docs/CRED003_FLIGHTRECORDER_SANITIZATION_EVIDENCE.md`. | `REQ-DX-105`, `CRED003` |\n    46\t| **WP-1103** | **Versioned Evaluation Datasets** | Migrate `eval/tasks/` into structured datasets under `eval/datasets/`. Decouple task input specifications (`examples.jsonl`) from evaluation assertions (`oracles.jsonl`). Add versioning and dataset splits (`regression`, `benchmark`). | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.3 |\n    47\t| **WP-1104** | **Standalone `nexus eval` Command** | Implement `nexus eval` subcommand in launcher grammar, supporting `--dataset <path>`, `--runs <count>`, `--isolated-home`, and structured JSON score outputs. | `REQ-EVL-101`, `ROADMAP.md` |\n    48\t| **WP-1105** | **Deterministic Code Evaluators** | Implement modular evaluator library in `eval/evaluators/code/`: AST syntax validation, build pass/fail, typecheck exit codes, diff boundary compliance, and JSON repair rates. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §4.1 |\n    49\t| **WP-1106** | **Single Step Loop Mode** | Implement `--step` flag in `nexus run` and `/step` REPL command to execute one agent turn and pause deterministically for operator confirmation. | `REQ-AGT-111` |\n    50\t| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\n    51\t| **WP-1108** | **Zero Technical Debt & Dependency Modernization** | Triage, validate, and integrate the 27 post-v1.0.0 Dependabot PRs (#103–#129) under an absolute zero-deprecation policy for third-party libraries. Categorized across 5 staged batches: Core Rust runtime (#105, #107, #110, #113), GitHub Actions CI workflows (#103, #104, #106, #108, #112), Cloudflare micro-workers (#109, #115–#118, #121–#123, #125–#128), TypeScript compiler (#119, #124, #129), and CLI runtime migrations (#111, #114, #120 including Commander 12→15 compatibility audit). Enforces continuous zero-technical-debt invariants. | PRs #103–#129, `ROADMAP.md` §2.1 |\n    52\t\n    53\t### v1.1.0 Release Gates\n    54\t\n    55\t- **Gate G1.1-1 (Zero-Leak Tracing):** Local trace engine produces valid OTel GenAI spans for all turn steps without leaking environment credentials or writing outside `~/.local/share/nexus/traces/`.\n    56\t- **Gate G1.1-2 (Dataset Decoupling):** Evaluator executes 100% of benchmark tasks with zero leakage of `oracles.jsonl` to agent prompt context.\n    57\t- **Gate G1.1-3 (CLI Parity):** `nexus eval` executes cleanly from packaged binary installations without developer dependencies.\n    58\t- **Gate G1.1-4 (Constrained Decoding Reliability):** GBNF-constrained execution achieves >=99.5% valid JSON tool call syntax (minimizing syntax repair retries) across supported local inference endpoints (llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama).\n    59\t- **Gate G1.1-5 (Zero Technical Debt & Zero Deprecated Packages):** Strictly 0 deprecated packages, 0 unmaintained dependencies, 0 CodeQL alerts, and 0 compiler warnings repository-wide. All 27 Dependabot PR upgrades pass unit/PTY suites, `cargo deny check`, automated npm registry deprecation scans, package reproducibility (`cmp`), and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants.\n    60\t\n    61\t### 2.1 Dependabot Triage & Integration Matrix (WP-1108)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":730376801}},"started_at_ms":1793622400972,"completed_at_ms":1793622401703}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:26:42.885Z","ordinal":42366,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19c39-e744-7b73-9363-17bf5b6ce467","call_id":"call_1245a590701d449ba896365cfa4e5ba6","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3918)\nTotal output lines: 62\n\n    65\t- **RED:** Strengthened `packaged evaluator runtime executes outside checkout` to invoke the packaged CLI and actual runner/scorer against a valid empty dataset; it failed because `eval/run.mjs` did not create `results.jsonl` when the selected split had no tasks.\n    66\t- **GREEN:** Pinned Bookworm package build completed; after extraction outside the checkout, `node --test eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` passed 3/3 with the actual installed `nexus eval` CLI, runner, and scorer. The rebuilt development artifact is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.1.tar.gz`; it is not exact-commit release evidence.\n    67\t- **Peer review:** Independent code review returned `APPROVED_WITH_COMMENTS` for AC2. Reviewer confirmed the installed CLI/runner/scorer path and the empty-split file fix; the comment is blocking AC4 evidence, which remains outstanding.\n    68\t- **AC3 test review:** A second independent read-only review confirmed that passing an invalid `NEXUS_HOME` and asserting the explicit `--limit` diagnostic wins establishes validation-before-runtime-resolution; assertions cover the score parent, score file and artifact directory remaining absent. The focused test has not yet been run because another worktree's test process is still live.\n    69\t- **AC5 test review:** An independent read-only review confirmed the non-empty two-task fixture and `--limit 1` assertions exercise real truncation and first-task-only prompting. The reviewer caught that `spawnSync` would block the in-process mock server; the test now uses async `spawn`, which the reviewer confirmed resolves that deadlock. Runtime verification remains pending the shared test lane.\n    70\t- **AC5 red/green:** The first strengthened run failed because the mock returned JSON while the client requested SSE (`INFERENCE_FAILED: stream_incomplete`). After switching to the retrieved SSE contract and setting `--workspace` to an isolated empty directory (so evaluator discovery cannot run this repository's test suite), `node cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs test/eval_cli.test.ts` passed 7/7; the non-empty `--limit 1` case confirmed exactly one completion request containing the first prompt and not the second.\n    71\t- **Six-task installed-candidate acceptance (2026-11-02):** The new `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance` acceptance test first failed with the expected missing-evidence assertion. A diagnostic run also confirmed that extracting an installed runtime below `/tmp` is rejected by the existing runtime root policy, so the test now extracts the archive into a fresh safe worktree path outside `/tmp` and the source checkout. A pinned Bookworm package was built from this integration worktree and its exact installed `bin/nexus` ran the `core-v1` benchmark split through a loopback deterministic fake provider. Focused test passed: 6/6 task invocations, 6 captured requests, no skipped or missing tasks, recomputed manifest SHA `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`; archive SHA `b385cd533f9e14bb161dba9a352d310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a`. Per-task hidden/regression validator and scorer outputs are retained in candidate-specific `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-b385cd533f9e.json`. The earlier generic `acceptance.json` is retained unchanged as superseded evidence; the test writes candidate evidence exclusively and rejects relative `hidden/...` command paths as well as full hidden validator commands in captured requests. This acceptance establishes execution coverage and request capture only; the deterministic `task_completed` fixture does not establish model quality, and its expected hidden checks are recorded as false.\n    72\t- **Independent review:** Initial re-review returned `REQUEST_CHANGES` to close WP-1103/1104 because six-task installed-candidate evidence was absent. Review of the first evidence found the relative hidden-command assertion too weak and the evidence write non-exclusive; both findings were addressed and the focused acceptance test passed again with candidate-specific evidence. Fresh full-slice re-review is pending.\n    73\t\n    74\t## Gate attempt notes\n    75\t\n    76\t- **Global release-scope guard:** Current `docs/releases/v1.1.2.md` still defines v1.1.2 as a patch on v1.1.1 containing one operation-message fix and inheriting v1.1.1 qualification. `docs/v1.1.0/README.md` also says WP-11x…1718 tokens truncated…hed.\nnl: docs/v1.1.0/WP-1108-TRIAGE.md: No such file or directory\n    40\t### Work Packages\n    41\t\n    42\t| ID | Title | Summary & Deliverables | Backlog / Audit Source |\n    43\t| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n    44\t| **WP-1101** | **OpenTelemetry Local Tracing** | Implement `cli/src/core/trace.ts` providing hierarchical tracing conforming to OpenTelemetry GenAI semantics. Captures agent turn roots, model request spans, tool execution spans, and context compactions into local `trace.jsonl` files. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.1 |\n    45\t| **WP-1102** | **Flight Recorder Credential Redaction** | Implement automated zero-leak credential sanitization across all recorded spans, CLI error dumps, and debug journals, validating against the test fixtures in `docs/CRED003_FLIGHTRECORDER_SANITIZATION_EVIDENCE.md`. | `REQ-DX-105`, `CRED003` |\n    46\t| **WP-1103** | **Versioned Evaluation Datasets** | Migrate `eval/tasks/` into structured datasets under `eval/datasets/`. Decouple task input specifications (`examples.jsonl`) from evaluation assertions (`oracles.jsonl`). Add versioning and dataset splits (`regression`, `benchmark`). | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.3 |\n    47\t| **WP-1104** | **Standalone `nexus eval` Command** | Implement `nexus eval` subcommand in launcher grammar, supporting `--dataset <path>`, `--runs <count>`, `--isolated-home`, and structured JSON score outputs. | `REQ-EVL-101`, `ROADMAP.md` |\n    48\t| **WP-1105** | **Deterministic Code Evaluators** | Implement modular evaluator library in `eval/evaluators/code/`: AST syntax validation, build pass/fail, typecheck exit codes, diff boundary compliance, and JSON repair rates. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §4.1 |\n    49\t| **WP-1106** | **Single Step Loop Mode** | Implement `--step` flag in `nexus run` and `/step` REPL command to execute one agent turn and pause deterministically for operator confirmation. | `REQ-AGT-111` |\n    50\t| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\n    51\t| **WP-1108** | **Zero Technical Debt & Dependency Modernization** | Triage, validate, and integrate the 27 post-v1.0.0 Dependabot PRs (#103–#129) under an absolute zero-deprecation policy for third-party libraries. Categorized across 5 staged batches: Core Rust runtime (#105, #107, #110, #113), GitHub Actions CI workflows (#103, #104, #106, #108, #112), Cloudflare micro-workers (#109, #115–#118, #121–#123, #125–#128), TypeScript compiler (#119, #124, #129), and CLI runtime migrations (#111, #114, #120 including Commander 12→15 compatibility audit). Enforces continuous zero-technical-debt invariants. | PRs #103–#129, `ROADMAP.md` §2.1 |\n    52\t\n    53\t### v1.1.0 Release Gates\n    54\t\n    55\t- **Gate G1.1-1 (Zero-Leak Tracing):** Local trace engine produces valid OTel GenAI spans for all turn steps without leaking environment credentials or writing outside `~/.local/share/nexus/traces/`.\n    56\t- **Gate G1.1-2 (Dataset Decoupling):** Evaluator executes 100% of benchmark tasks with zero leakage of `oracles.jsonl` to agent prompt context.\n    57\t- **Gate G1.1-3 (CLI Parity):** `nexus eval` executes cleanly from packaged binary installations without developer dependencies.\n    58\t- **Gate G1.1-4 (Constrained Decoding Reliability):** GBNF-constrained execution achieves >=99.5% valid JSON tool call syntax (minimizing syntax repair retries) across supported local inference endpoints (llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama).\n    59\t- **Gate G1.1-5 (Zero Technical Debt & Zero Deprecated Packages):** Strictly 0 deprecated packages, 0 unmaintained dependencies, 0 CodeQL alerts, and 0 compiler warnings repository-wide. All 27 Dependabot PR upgrades pass unit/PTY suites, `cargo deny check`, automated npm registry deprecation scans, package reproducibility (`cmp`), and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants.\n    60\t\n    61\t### 2.1 Dependabot Triage & Integration Matrix (WP-1108)\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19c35-8dbf-7b72-9a43-c0e91b05ed32","create_time":1793622402.8849022}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
