{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:42:52.632Z","ordinal":42836,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a19c48-b357-77c2-91b3-b22b3908d2c7","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUESTED.** G1.1-5’s required proof is missing one explicit roadmap condition: CLI option compatibility must be demonstrated **without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants**. The gate row at line 28 says “CLI compatibility” but doesn’t preserve that security boundary. Please include the invariant in both the required-proof text and the remaining-evidence checklist so compatibility cannot be marked complete without it."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19c45-79f8-74d0-bea2-bdff6a04336d","create_time":1793623372.6319182,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":1752}}
