{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:59:28.528Z","ordinal":43440,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a19c57-e590-7b82-b72c-6b637d3fdc54","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUESTED** for the evidence file; the test and plan addendum otherwise address the AC2 mount-view gap.\n\nReviewed state: branch `v1/v112-wp1104-integration` at `2a94f62e`, with uncommitted changes to `cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts` and `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md`, plus untracked `acceptance-b385cd533f9e-ac2-suite.json`. I did not run tests.\n\nThe test exercises the real candidate’s `run_command` path and checks fixture visibility, the `/workspace` mount, absence of the dataset staging root from mountinfo, and unreadability of the absolute synthetic validator path. Existing relative-path and sentinel checks remain. I found no source-level AC2 gap.\n\nThe new evidence file is misleading: it is byte-identical (SHA-256 `e4c16f8d…315f37fd`) to three existing six-task acceptance files and contains no suite result, log reference, or mount-probe results. Since the full suite failed, don’t label this duplicate as AC2 suite evidence. Remove it or make it an accurate record of the failed suite run, distinct from the six-task acceptance evidence. The current full-suite result remains **failed/unqualified**."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19c45-79f8-74d0-bea2-bdff6a04336d","create_time":1793624368.5283802,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":1789}}
