{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:59:37.667Z","ordinal":43449,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a19c58-0943-71b1-bbae-b9db71ef8886","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Current: 2026-11-02 12:59pm UTC\nThis file has prior observations — supplementary context follows. The Read result below is the full requested section.\n- **Need details on a past observation?** get_observations([IDs]) — ~300 tokens each.\n- **Need a structural map first?** smart_outline(\"docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-b385cd533f9e-ac2-suite.json\") — line numbers only, cheaper than re-reading.\n### Nov 2, 2026\n27556 12:22p 🔵 WP-1103 Integration Worktree Has Untracked AC2 Suite Acceptance Evidence File"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19c45-79f8-74d0-bea2-bdff6a04336d","create_time":1793624377.6678097,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:59:38.858Z","ordinal":43450,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19c45-79f8-74d0-bea2-bdff6a04336d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-bab34e02-23fb-4887-9387-728176cc8a37","process_id":"58027","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'acceptance-b385cd533f9e-ac2-suite|b385cd533f9e|AC2' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md; cat docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-b385cd533f9e-ac2-suite.json; git diff -- cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n 'acceptance-b385cd533f9e-ac2-suite|b385cd533f9e|AC2' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md; cat docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-b385cd533f9e-ac2-suite.json; git diff -- cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"10:- **AC2:** The candidate's staged workspace and declared filesystem/mount view expose the task fixture repository but do not expose the dataset task directory or hidden validator files by path or content. Test: `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`.\n18:**Dependencies:** WP-1103 versioned dataset loader and runner integration; current runner claims are held by root after the prior claim was recorded stale and broken; a test seam for AC1, AC2 and AC4. AC5 requires an integrated exact-candidate benchmark run and is separate from the unit regression suite; packaged installed CLI behavior depends on WP-1104.\n39:## AC2 plan addendum — actual candidate mount view\n41:**Spec refinement:** AC2 requires evidence from the running dataset candidate's filesystem view, in addition to proving that the staged fixture workspace omits hidden files. The test must show that the candidate can see its declared `/workspace` mount, that the evaluator's dataset staging root is not mounted there, and that the absolute hidden validator path is unreadable.\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"candidate\": {\n    \"packageArchiveSha256\": \"b385cd533f9e14bb161dba9a352d310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a\",\n    \"launcherSha256\": \"320d7dc1603d30f863a9560a9101ab3fe1a57f164b7119c49e01d9ace40792c4\",\n    \"cliBundleSha256\": \"054d8e1ca616020227920d9e2bfb9f1152f4c135b0539fee42e4451bec0f08fb\",\n    \"coreBinarySha256\": \"57cc67889a919f7cc3c98e44d416faa91a49ed66f64992128a7fa1adeb61fedd\"\n  },\n  \"dataset\": {\n    \"name\": \"core-v1\",\n    \"version\": \"1.1.0\",\n    \"split\": \"benchmark\",\n    \"manifestSha256\": \"05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43\",\n    \"manifestSha256Source\": \"recomputed from final integrated eval/datasets/core-v1/manifest.json\"\n  },\n  \"provider\": {\n    \"kind\": \"loopback-deterministic-fake\",\n    \"capturedRequests\": 6\n  },\n  \"expectedTaskIds\": [\n    \"t2-bugfix-csv\",\n    \"t2-bugfix-duration\",\n    \"t2-debug-logs\",\n    \"t2-feature-inventory\",\n    \"t2-feature-slugify\",\n    \"t2-refactor-tax\"\n  ],\n  \"missingTaskIds\": [],\n  \"skippedTaskIds\": [],\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"taskId\": \"t2-bugfix-csv\",\n      \"invocations\": 1,\n      \"requestSha256\": \"0ecfa5104ddb0efbbf09d90c71c9d46bf21a30ecbec994a8db780dd18a086e44\",\n      \"validatorResult\": {\n        \"hiddenPass\": false,\n        \"regressionPass\": false,\n        \"exitCode\": 0,\n        \"timedOut\": false\n      },\n      \"scorerResult\": {\n        \"claimed\": 1,\n        \"correct\": 0,\n        \"errors\": 0,\n        \"regressions\": 1\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"taskId\": \"t2-bugfix-duration\",\n      \"invocations\": 1,\n      \"requestSha256\": \"09ae06956013a429b999ac14ad2e844df3c60be8a312a1ef0909d9c615fb772f\",\n      \"validatorResult\": {\n        \"hiddenPass\": false,\n        \"regressionPass\": false,\n        \"exitCode\": 0,\n        \"timedOut\": false\n      },\n      \"scorerResult\": {\n        \"claimed\": 1,\n        \"correct\": 0,\n        \"errors\": 0,\n        \"regressions\": 1\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"taskId\": \"t2-debug-logs\",\n      \"invocations\": 1,\n      \"requestSha256\": \"57f5474b1e2f4fb89e7d8a307f559a10e4612f384d7c86299a711b4f2d7a8f65\",\n      \"validatorResult\": {\n        \"hiddenPass\": false,\n        \"regressionPass\": true,\n        \"exitCode\": 0,\n        \"timedOut\": false\n      },\n      \"scorerResult\": {\n        \"claimed\": 1,\n        \"correct\": 0,\n        \"errors\": 0,\n        \"regressions\": 0\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"taskId\": \"t2-feature-inventory\",\n      \"invocations\": 1,\n      \"requestSha256\": \"b2a2cd4c817f62a5f60555b6ad93efb29d40fe0c72eac03d2439328d6f3415f2\",\n      \"validatorResult\": {\n        \"hiddenPass\": false,\n        \"regressionPass\": true,\n        \"exitCode\": 0,\n        \"timedOut\": false\n      },\n      \"scorerResult\": {\n        \"claimed\": 1,\n        \"correct\": 0,\n        \"errors\": 0,\n        \"regressions\": 0\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"taskId\": \"t2-feature-slugify\",\n      \"invocations\": 1,\n      \"requestSha256\": \"f4eb7d9fa1cec06e9c1063ecad66492e0375c0a1bb93d02a55f2817294ca9b41\",\n      \"validatorResult\": {\n        \"hiddenPass\": false,\n        \"regressionPass\": true,\n        \"exitCode\": 0,\n        \"timedOut\": false\n      },\n      \"scorerResult\": {\n        \"claimed\": 1,\n        \"correct\": 0,\n        \"errors\": 0,\n        \"regressions\": 0\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"taskId\": \"t2-refactor-tax\",\n      \"invocations\": 1,\n      \"requestSha256\": \"c0fd5ceb25b0d39f62becfef32433d9683c24d665b032229304c0507237e3710\",\n      \"validatorResult\": {\n        \"hiddenPass\": false,\n        \"regressionPass\": true,\n        \"exitCode\": 0,\n        \"timedOut\": false\n      },\n      \"scorerResult\": {\n        \"claimed\": 1,\n        \"correct\": 0,\n        \"errors\": 0,\n        \"regressions\": 0\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\ndiff --git a/cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts b/cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts\nindex c82e93f5..fb7af3b3 100644\n--- a/cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts\n+++ b/cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts\n@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@ test(\"versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels\", {\n   const sentinel = \"ORACLE_SENTINEL_WP1103_PRIVATE_VALIDATOR\";\n   const root = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-dataset-cli-test-\"));\n   const dataset = path.join(root, \"dataset\");\n+  const absoluteHiddenPath = path.join(dataset, \"tasks\", \"selftest-add\", \"hidden\", \"math.hidden.test.js\");\n   const gateway = await startGateway((request, body) => {\n     const toolCount = (body?.messages ?? []).filter((message: any) => message.role === \"tool\").length;\n     const calls = toolCount === 0\n@@ -35,6 +36,8 @@ test(\"versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels\", {\n       : toolCount === 1\n         ? [{ name: \"read_file\", args: { path: \"hidden/math.hidden.test.js\" } }]\n         : toolCount === 2\n+          ? [{ name: \"run_command\", args: { command: `if test -f package.json; then printf 'DATASET_TEST_FIXTURE_REPO_VISIBLE\\\\n'; else printf 'DATASET_TEST_FIXTURE_REPO_MISSING\\\\n'; fi; if grep -F ' /workspace ' /proc/self/mountinfo >/dev/null; then printf 'DATASET_TEST_WORKSPACE_MOUNT_PRESENT\\\\n'; else printf 'DATASET_TEST_WORKSPACE_MOUNT_MISSING\\\\n'; fi; if grep -F ' ${dataset} ' /proc/self/mountinfo >/dev/null; then printf 'DATASET_ROOT_MOUNT_PRESENT\\\\n'; else printf 'DATASET_ROOT_MOUNT_ABSENT\\\\n'; fi; if test -r '${absoluteHiddenPath}'; then printf 'DATASET_ABSOLUTE_HIDDEN_PATH_READABLE\\\\n'; cat '${absoluteHiddenPath}'; else printf 'DATASET_ABSOLUTE_HIDDEN_PATH_UNREADABLE\\\\n'; fi`, timeout_secs: 10 } }]\n+          : toolCount === 3\n         ? [{ name: \"write_file\", args: { path: \"math.js\", content: \"exports.add = (a, b) => a + b;\\n\" } }]\n         : [{ name: \"task_completed\", args: { summary: \"math.js added\" } }];\n     return { kind: \"tools\", calls };\n@@ -86,6 +89,15 @@ test(\"versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels\", {\n       assert.ok(toolResults.every((message: any) => !JSON.stringify(message).includes(sentinel)), \"oracle sentinel never reaches a candidate tool result\");\n       assert.ok(!JSON.stringify(toolResults[0]).includes(\"math.hidden.test.js\"), \"candidate workspace tree excludes hidden validator path\");\n       assert.ok(toolResults.some((message: any) => /not found|does not exist|no such file/i.test(String(message.content))), \"candidate cannot read the evaluator-only hidden validator path\");\n+      const mountProbeMessage = toolResults.find((message: any) => message.name === \"run_command\");\n+      assert.ok(mountProbeMessage, \"the candidate executed the dataset mount-view probe\");\n+      const mountProbe = JSON.parse(mountProbeMessage.content);\n+      assert.equal(mountProbe.exit_code, 0, mountProbe.stderr);\n+      assert.match(mountProbe.stdout, /DATASET_TEST_FIXTURE_REPO_VISIBLE/, \"the candidate sees the fixture repository it must work in\");\n+      assert.match(mountProbe.stdout, /DATASET_TEST_WORKSPACE_MOUNT_PRESENT/, \"the candidate observes its declared workspace mount\");\n+      assert.match(mountProbe.stdout, /DATASET_ROOT_MOUNT_ABSENT/, \"the dataset staging root is absent from the candidate mount view\");\n+      assert.match(mountProbe.stdout, /DATASET_ABSOLUTE_HIDDEN_PATH_UNREADABLE/, \"the absolute evaluator validator path cannot be read by the candidate\");\n+      assert.doesNotMatch(mountProbe.stdout, /DATASET_ABSOLUTE_HIDDEN_PATH_READABLE|ORACLE_SENTINEL_WP1103_PRIVATE_VALIDATOR/, \"the evaluator validator path and sentinel never enter candidate-visible output\");\n     });\n     await t.test(\"versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit\", () => {\n       assert.equal(records[0].hiddenPass, true, `root=${root} ${JSON.stringify(records[0])}`);\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md b/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md\nindex 3f03ed29..1da901ec 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md\n@@ -35,3 +35,13 @@\n **Risk / unknown:** The current runner merges example and oracle fields into an evaluator-side task record before launching the candidate. The exact prompt/provider request and candidate filesystem/mount boundary must be observed without a live model; the fake provider/request capture must establish the actual CLI prompt path, and filesystem checks must establish access denial rather than mere omission from the staged copy. The benchmark evidence must identify the exact candidate SHA, dataset version, split, manifest SHA-256, denominator and each task invocation/result.\n \n **Coordination:** The original plan was independently approved by `review_delta` and `release_gate_audit`. The previous runner claim was older than 24 hours, its clean branch was still `c548e53e`, the host had rebooted since the claim, and no process had its worktree as cwd; `.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log` records the stale-claim break at 2026-11-01T21:56Z. Old dataset and runner branches are preserved as read-only reference. Fresh claims now point to `v1/v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` at `origin/main` 593d569b. Re-review this updated plan before coding. The previous SUITE claim was released after host reboot interrupted its run; claim SUITE before the next suite.\n+\n+## AC2 plan addendum — actual candidate mount view\n+\n+**Spec refinement:** AC2 requires evidence from the running dataset candidate's filesystem view, in addition to proving that the staged fixture workspace omits hidden files. The test must show that the candidate can see its declared `/workspace` mount, that the evaluator's dataset staging root is not mounted there, and that the absolute hidden validator path is unreadable.\n+\n+**Chunk:** Extend the existing `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` subtest in `cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts`. Use the local fake provider to ask the real candidate to execute a read-only `run_command` probe. Capture the command's stdout and assert all three mount/path outcomes, while retaining the existing relative-path and sentinel assertions. No production sandbox change is planned unless the probe exposes a real leak.\n+\n+**Reference retrieval:** XERJ `nexus-cli/sandbox.ts:183` (`probeBwrapSandbox`) demonstrates probing a real Bubblewrap process against an outside canary; `nexus-cli/tools.ts:1523` locates the production `run_command` wrapper, and `nexus-cli/sandbox.ts:219` provides the `wrapSandboxedCommand` signature. `eval/isolate.mjs` is outside the indexed CLI source; local source inspection at `agentSandboxArgv` confirmed the evaluator mounts `/tmp` as tmpfs and binds the candidate workspace at `/workspace`.\n+\n+**Observed TDD:** The first focused run failed because the assertion matched the literal readable branch in the captured command rather than its stdout. The test was corrected to parse the `run_command` result. The focused dataset test then passed 3/3, with workspace mount present, dataset root mount absent, and the absolute validator path unreadable. This change adds dataset-specific acceptance evidence; it does not change production sandbox code.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":11145795}},"started_at_ms":1793624377846,"completed_at_ms":1793624378857}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:59:40.702Z","ordinal":43451,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19c58-151e-7ae0-b29b-707468763820","call_id":"call_653acd5b63f842ebafe2750cfc708b26","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"10:- **AC2:** The candidate's staged workspace and declared filesystem/mount view expose the task fixture repository but do not expose the dataset task directory or hidden validator files by path or content. Test: `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`.\n18:**Dependencies:** WP-1103 versioned dataset loader and runner integration; current runner claims are held by root after the prior claim was recorded stale and broken; a test seam for AC1, AC2 and AC4. AC5 requires an integrated exact-candidate benchmark run and is separate from the unit regression suite; packaged installed CLI behavior depends on WP-1104.\n39:## AC2 plan addendum — actual candidate mount view\n41:**Spec refinement:** AC2 requires evidence from the running dataset candidate's filesystem view, in addition to proving that the staged fixture workspace omits hidden files. The test must show that the candidate can see its declared `/workspace` mount, that the evaluator's dataset staging root is not mounted there, and that the absolute hidden validator path is unreadable.\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"candidate\": {\n    \"packageArchiveSha256\": \"b385cd533f9e14bb161dba9a352d310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a\",\n    \"launcherSha256\": \"320d7dc1603d30f863a9560a9101ab3fe1a57f164b7119c49e01d9ace40792c4\",\n    \"cliBundleSha256\": \"054d8e1ca616020227920d9e2bfb9f1152f4c135b0539fee42e4451bec0f08fb\",\n    \"coreBinarySha256\": \"57cc67889a919f7cc3c98e44d416faa91a49ed66f64992128a7fa1adeb61fedd\"\n  },\n  \"dataset\": {\n    \"name\": \"core-v1\",\n    \"version\": \"1.1.0\",\n    \"split\": \"benchmark\",\n    \"manifestSha256\": \"05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43\",\n    \"manifestSha256Source\": \"recomputed from final integrated eval/datasets/core-v1/manifest.json\"\n  },\n  \"provider\": {\n    \"kind\": \"loopback-deterministic-fake\",\n    \"capturedRequests\": 6\n  },\n  \"expectedTaskIds\": [\n    \"t2-bugfix-csv\",\n    \"t2-bugfix-duration\",\n    \"t2-debug-logs\",\n    \"t2-feature-inventory\",\n    \"t2-feature-slugify\",\n    \"t2-refactor-tax\"\n  ],\n  \"missingTaskIds\": [],\n  \"skippedTaskIds\": [],\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"taskId\": \"t2-bugfix-csv\",\n      \"invocations\": 1,\n      \"requestSha256\": \"0ecfa5104ddb0efbbf09d90c71c9d46bf21a30ecbec994a8db780dd18a086e44\",\n      \"validatorResult\": {\n        \"hiddenPass\": false,\n        \"regressionPass\": false,\n        \"exitCode\": 0,\n        \"timedOut\": false\n      },\n      \"scorerResult\": {\n        \"claimed\": 1,\n        \"correct\": 0,\n        \"errors\": 0,\n        \"regressions\": 1\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"taskId\": \"t2-bugfix-duration\",\n      \"invocations\": 1,\n      \"requestSha256\": \"09ae06956013a429b999ac14ad2e844df3c60be8a312a1ef0909d9c615fb772f\",\n      \"validatorResult\": {\n        \"hiddenPass\": false,\n        \"regressionPass\": false,\n        \"exitCode\": 0,\n        \"timedOut\": false\n      },\n      \"scorerResult\": {\n        \"claimed\": 1,\n        \"correct\": 0,\n        \"errors\": 0,\n        \"regressions\": 1\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"taskId\": \"t2-debug-logs\",\n      \"invocations\": 1,\n      \"requestSha256\": \"57f5474b1e2f4fb89e7d8a307f559a10e4612f384d7c86299a711b4f2d7a8f65\",\n      \"validatorResult\": {\n        \"hiddenPass\": false,\n        \"regressionPass\": true,\n        \"exitCode\": 0,\n        \"timedOut\": false\n      },\n      \"scorerResult\": {\n        \"claimed\": 1,\n        \"correct\": 0,\n        \"errors\": 0,\n        \"regressions\": 0\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"taskId\": \"t2-feature-inventory\",\n      \"invocations\": 1,\n      \"requestSha256\": \"b2a2cd4c817f62a5f60555b6ad93efb29d40fe0c72eac03d2439328d6f3415f2\",\n      \"validatorResult\": {\n        \"hiddenPass\": false,\n        \"regressionPass\": true,\n        \"exitCode\": 0,\n        \"timedOut\": false\n      },\n      \"scorerResult\": {\n        \"claimed\": 1,\n        \"correct\": 0,\n        \"errors\": 0,\n        \"regressions\": 0\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"taskId\": \"t2-feature-slugify\",\n      \"invocations\": 1,\n      \"requestSha256\": \"f4eb7d9fa1cec06e9c1063ecad66492e0375c0a1bb93d02a55f2817294ca9b41\",\n      \"validatorResult\": {\n        \"hiddenPass\": false,\n        \"regressionPass\": true,\n        \"exitCode\": 0,\n        \"timedOut\": false\n      },\n      \"scorerResult\": {\n        \"claimed\": 1,\n        \"correct\": 0,\n        \"errors\": 0,\n        \"regressions\": 0\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"taskId\": \"t2-refactor-tax\",\n      \"invocations\": 1,\n      \"requestSha256\": \"c0fd5ceb25b0d39f62becfef32433d9683c24d665b032229304c0507237e3710\",\n      \"validatorResult\": {\n        \"hiddenPass\": false,\n        \"regressionPass\": true,\n        \"exitCode\": 0,\n        \"timedOut\": false\n      },\n      \"scorerResult\": {\n        \"claimed\": 1,\n        \"correct\": 0,\n        \"errors\": 0,\n        \"regressions\": 0\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\ndiff --git a/cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts b/cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts\nindex c82e93f5..fb7af3b3 100644\n--- a/cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts\n+++ b/cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts\n@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@ test(\"versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels\", {\n   const sentinel = \"ORACLE_SENTINEL_WP1103_PRIVATE_VALIDATOR\";\n   const root = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-dataset-cli-test-\"));\n   const dataset = path.join(root, \"dataset\");\n+  const absoluteHiddenPath = path.join(dataset, \"tasks\", \"selftest-add\", \"hidden\", \"math.hidden.test.js\");\n   const gateway = await startGateway((request, body) => {\n     const toolCount = (body?.messages ?? []).filter((message: any) => message.role === \"tool\").length;\n     const calls = toolCount === 0\n@@ -35,6 +36,8 @@ test(\"versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels\", {\n       : toolCount === 1\n         ? [{ name: \"read_file\", args: { path: \"hidden/math.hidden.test.js\" } }]\n         : toolCount === 2\n+          ? [{ name: \"run_command\", args: { command: `if test -f package.json; then printf 'DATASET_TEST_FIXTURE_REPO_VISIBLE\\\\n'; else printf 'DATASET_TEST_FIXTURE_REPO_MISSING\\\\n'; fi; if grep -F ' /workspace ' /proc/self/mountinfo >/dev/null; then printf 'DATASET_TEST_WORKSPACE_MOUNT_PRESENT\\\\n'; else printf 'DATASET_TEST_WORKSPACE_MOUNT_MISSING\\\\n'; fi; if grep -F ' ${dataset} ' /proc/self/mountinfo >/dev/null; then printf 'DATASET_ROOT_MOUNT_PRESENT\\\\n'; else printf 'DATASET_ROOT_MOUNT_ABSENT\\\\n'; fi; if test -r '${absoluteHiddenPath}'; then printf 'DATASET_ABSOLUTE_HIDDEN_PATH_READABLE\\\\n'; cat '${absoluteHiddenPath}'; else printf 'DATASET_ABSOLUTE_HIDDEN_PATH_UNREADABLE\\\\n'; fi`, timeout_secs: 10 } }]\n+          : toolCount === 3\n         ? [{ name: \"write_file\", args: { path: \"math.js\", content: \"exports.add = (a, b) => a + b;\\n\" } }]\n         : [{ name: \"task_completed\", args: { summary: \"math.js added\" } }];\n     return { kind: \"tools\", calls };\n@@ -86,6 +89,15 @@ test(\"versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels\", {\n       assert.ok(toolResults.every((message: any) => !JSON.stringify(message).includes(sentinel)), \"oracle sentinel never reaches a candidate tool result\");\n       assert.ok(!JSON.stringify(toolResults[0]).includes(\"math.hidden.test.js\"), \"candidate workspace tree excludes hidden validator path\");\n       assert.ok(toolResults.some((message: any) => /not found|does not exist|no such file/i.test(String(message.content))), \"candidate cannot read the evaluator-only hidden validator path\");\n+      const mountProbeMessage = toolResults.find((message: any) => message.name === \"run_command\");\n+      assert.ok(mountProbeMessage, \"the candidate executed the dataset mount-view probe\");\n+      const mountProbe = JSON.parse(mountProbeMessage.content);\n+      assert.equal(mountProbe.exit_code, 0, mountProbe.stderr);\n+      assert.match(mountProbe.stdout, /DATASET_TEST_FIXTURE_REPO_VISIBLE/, \"the candidate sees the fixture repository it must work in\");\n+      assert.match(mountProbe.stdout, /DATASET_TEST_WORKSPACE_MOUNT_PRESENT/, \"the candidate observes its declared workspace mount\");\n+      assert.match(mountProbe.stdout, /DATASET_ROOT_MOUNT_ABSENT/, \"the dataset staging root is absent from the candidate mount view\");\n+      assert.match(mountProbe.stdout, /DATASET_ABSOLUTE_HIDDEN_PATH_UNREADABLE/, \"the absolute evaluator validator path cannot be read by the candidate\");\n+      assert.doesNotMatch(mountProbe.stdout, /DATASET_ABSOLUTE_HIDDEN_PATH_READABLE|ORACLE_SENTINEL_WP1103_PRIVATE_VALIDATOR/, \"the evaluator validator path and sentinel never enter candidate-visible output\");\n     });\n     await t.test(\"versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit\", () => {\n       assert.equal(records[0].hiddenPass, true, `root=${root} ${JSON.stringify(records[0])}`);\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md b/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md\nindex 3f03ed29..1da901ec 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md\n@@ -35,3 +35,13 @@\n **Risk / unknown:** The current runner merges example and oracle fields into an evaluator-side task record before launching the candidate. The exact prompt/provider request and candidate filesystem/mount boundary must be observed without a live model; the fake provider/request capture must establish the actual CLI prompt path, and filesystem checks must establish access denial rather than mere omission from the staged copy. The benchmark evidence must identify the exact candidate SHA, dataset version, split, manifest SHA-256, denominator and each task invocation/result.\n \n **Coordination:** The original plan was independently approved by `review_delta` and `release_gate_audit`. The previous runner claim was older than 24 hours, its clean branch was still `c548e53e`, the host had rebooted since the claim, and no process had its worktree as cwd; `.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log` records the stale-claim break at 2026-11-01T21:56Z. Old dataset and runner branches are preserved as read-only reference. Fresh claims now point to `v1/v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` at `origin/main` 593d569b. Re-review this updated plan before coding. The previous SUITE claim was released after host reboot interrupted its run; claim SUITE before the next suite.\n+\n+## AC2 plan addendum — actual candidate mount view\n+\n+**Spec refinement:** AC2 requires evidence from the running dataset candidate's filesystem view, in addition to proving that the staged fixture workspace omits hidden files. The test must show that the candidate can see its declared `/workspace` mount, that the evaluator's dataset staging root is not mounted there, and that the absolute hidden validator path is unreadable.\n+\n+**Chunk:** Extend the existing `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` subtest in `cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts`. Use the local fake provider to ask the real candidate to execute a read-only `run_command` probe. Capture the command's stdout and assert all three mount/path outcomes, while retaining the existing relative-path and sentinel assertions. No production sandbox change is planned unless the probe exposes a real leak.\n+\n+**Reference retrieval:** XERJ `nexus-cli/sandbox.ts:183` (`probeBwrapSandbox`) demonstrates probing a real Bubblewrap process against an outside canary; `nexus-cli/tools.ts:1523` locates the production `run_command` wrapper, and `nexus-cli/sandbox.ts:219` provides the `wrapSandboxedCommand` signature. `eval/isolate.mjs` is outside the indexed CLI source; local source inspection at `agentSandboxArgv` confirmed the evaluator mounts `/tmp` as tmpfs and binds the candidate workspace at `/workspace`.\n+\n+**Observed TDD:** The first focused run failed because the assertion matched the literal readable branch in the captured command rather than its stdout. The test was corrected to parse the `run_command` result. The focused dataset test then passed 3/3, with workspace mount present, dataset root mount absent, and the absolute validator path unreadable. This change adds dataset-specific acceptance evidence; it does not change production sandbox code.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19c45-79f8-74d0-bea2-bdff6a04336d","create_time":1793624380.7025452}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
